{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMXsSUoDnuJaWaHU3UbGar","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n25:### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n33:### type AspectMode\n39:### BUILTIN_MODELS\n47:### chunkyResolution()\n55:### clearScene()\n63:### computeFraming()\n69:### countObjects()\n77:### type DebugAction\n87:### type DebugKeyChanges\n95:### type DebugKeyMap\n101:### type DebugKeysOption\n114:### DEFAULT_DEBUG_KEYS\n122:### disposeObject()\n132:### class Engine\n197:### ENGINE_VERSION\n203:### interface EngineOptions\n226:### FPS_OPTIONS\n232:### class FrameLimiter\n242:### frameView()\n253:### interface Framing\n266:### interface Game\n288:### interface GameContext\n305:### interface HeadlessOptions\n312:### class LoadingScreen\n323:### loadSettings()\n331:### normalizeSettings()\n339:### optionsFromUrl()\n352:### PIXEL_SIZES\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n372:### QUALITY\n381:### QUALITY_LEVELS\n387:### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n393:### type QualityLevel\n407:### type QualityOption\n413:### interface QualitySettings\n418:### rebindDebugKeys()\n428:### interface Resolution\n446:### RESOLUTIONS\n452:### resolveDebugKeys()\n460:### class Settings\n479:### interface SettingsHost\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n507:### storeSettings()\n513:### urlSettings()\n523:### interface Viewport\n531:### withUrlOptions()\n542:## 2. Camera\n544:### CAMERA_PRESETS\n550:### interface CameraConfig\n566:### type CameraPreset\n577:### class CameraRig\n604:### interface CameraRigState\n617:### createCameraRig()\n623:### class FirstPersonRig\n637:### class FreeRig\n655:### class OrthoRig\n666:### class ThirdPersonRig\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n679:### AMOUNT\n687:### applyFilter()\n696:### applyFilters()\n704:### type BackendName\n712:### interface CapturedFrame\n718:### clampParam()\n726:### cloneLook()\n732:### DEFAULT_EDGES\n738:### DEFAULT_PIXEL\n744:### defaultLook()\n752:### defaultParams()\n760:### interface EdgeSettings\n765:### FILTER_IDS\n771:### FILTER_PRESETS\n779:### interface FilterContext\n786:### interface FilterDef\n798:### type FilterGroup\n804:### filterOrder()\n812:### interface FilterParam\n824:### filterParams()\n832:### filterPresetOf()\n842:### filterPresets()\n850:### FILTERS\n856:### type FilterSpace\n862:### getFilter()\n868:### interface LayerLook\n875:### interface Look\n881:### LOOK_ALIASES\n889:### LOOK_PRESETS\n899:### LOOK_TARGET_LABELS\n905:### LOOK_TARGETS\n911:### interface LookFilter\n918:### lookFilters()\n926:### lookFromFilters()\n934:### type LookLayer\n942:### lookLayerOf()\n950:### interface LookPlan\n957:### lookPresetLabel()\n965:### lookPresetName()\n973:### lookPresetOf()\n981:### looksEqual()\n987:### type LookTarget\n995:### NO_WEBGPU\n1003:### normalizeLook()\n1013:### PALETTES\n1019:### paramsOf()\n1027:### PIXEL_PARAMS\n1033:### PIXEL_PRESETS\n1039:### interface PixelLook\n1047:### class PixelRenderer\n1103:### planLook()\n1112:### type RenderMode\n1118:### scenePixel()\n1126:### setLookLayer()\n1136:### splitFilters()\n1146:## 4. Materials, meshes and lights\n1148:### interface AssignItem\n1159:### class ContactShadow\n1169:### flicker()\n1178:### FLICKER_PRESETS\n1184:### type FlickerPreset\n1192:### glowMaterial()\n1203:### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n1211:### class LightAssigner\n1227:### interface LightHandle\n1249:### class LightPool\n1267:### interface LightPoolOptions\n1272:### interface LightPoolStats\n1281:### interface LightRequestOptions\n1297:### interface MergeOptions\n1302:### mergeStaticMeshes()\n1319:### PALETTE\n1329:### type PaletteColor\n1335:### pixelTexture()\n1343:### TOON_BANDS\n1352:### toonGradient()\n1358:### toonify()\n1368:### toonMaterial()\n1380:### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n1387:## 5. Physics\n1389:### interface BoxOptions\n1397:### interface Breakable\n1404:### interface BreakableOptions\n1417:### class Breakables\n1431:### interface BridgeOptions\n1441:### interface Built\n1448:### chain()\n1460:### interface ChainOptions\n1470:### type CharacterAnim\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n// check.mjs: play a Pixel Engine game in a real browser and report what happened.\n// Ships in the engine kit; run it before you hand a game back.\n//\n//   node check.mjs                       index.html in the current folder\n//   node check.mjs examples/looks.html   any page (served from the folder that holds pixel-engine.js)\n//   node check.mjs \"index.html?look=noir&camera=side\"   with URL flags\n//   node check.mjs http://localhost:5173/\n//   node check.mjs --sheets models.js    sheets of your own models and textures (no page played)\n//   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n//\n// Options:\n//   --keys KeyD*60,Space*4,KeyW*30   hold each key for that many frames, in order (default: 90 idle frames)\n//   --cameras                        also shoot the iso, topdown, side and third camera presets\n//   --looks pixel_heroes,noir        also shoot these looks (names from engine.lookPresets)\n//   --out check                      folder for the PNGs and report.json (default: ./check)\n//   --size 960x540                   viewport in CSS pixels\n//   --sheets models.js,crate,cobbles draw sheets instead of playing a page (ASSETS.md): every\n//                                    ModelDef and TextureDef a module exports (by name, in an\n//                                    array or object, in a ModelCatalog / TextureCatalog, or added\n//                                    to the library), and library ids. A PNG each and report.json\n//                                    in --out (default ./check/sheets); exit 1 on any problem\n//   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n//                                    page (no browser, no pictures): it imports the module, makes\n//                                    the game its `createGame()` export returns, plays the --keys\n//                                    frames, then replays that run's recording in a fresh game. It\n//                                    writes report.json (state, errors, fingerprint) to --out; exit\n//                                    1 on an error or a replay that ends somewhere else\n//   --help                           this text\n//\n// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n// `npx playwright install chromium`; a global install, `npm i -g playwright`, works too), or\n// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headless shell,\n// `chrome-linux/headless_shell`, is the lightest): it plays WebGPU on SwiftShader with no\n// display. Exit code 0 means the game started, ran the frames with no errors (page, console,\n// engine or GPU) and drew a picture (with --sheets: every sheet was drawn and no\n// def has a problem; warnings are fine); 1 means it didn't; 2 means the tool couldn't run (bad\n// arguments, no page, no browser, or a browser without WebGPU, which no game can start in).\nimport { execSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"app\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./game.js\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\ndocs:\nHUB-README.md\n\ntools:\nhub","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"d2acb2fe-7dd5-4bb9-aad9-897071ea5514","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:22:00.251Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Pixel Engine API