{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkh8mxKbquAP6xgjVYhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S6iNThBvXWjsTVa5PnpCud","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Status log\n- M0 done. Sim core written (src/sim/*, src/data/*): world/hero/effects/monsters/bosses/quests/knell/round/commands/bot/zonegen. Bot finishes the campaign in the sim for all 3 classes (`node .scratch/campaign.mjs <class>`), about 10 sim minutes, level 18-19.\n- tests/ISSUES.md gets one line per issue a test catches (needed for exit interview counts).\n\n## Architecture notes (for after compaction)\n- src/sim is plain JS, reads only Rng/NavGrid from the engine. stepWorld(w, intents[seat]). All menu actions go through applyCommand(w, seat, {c:..}) in sim/commands.js.\n- Sim emits events in w.events (t: spawn, hit, death, cast, mcast, fx, lob, shot, shotx, area, areax, tele, telex, wave, zone, quest, toast, sub, talk, open, cut, boss, drop, dropx, pick, level, ...). View consumes them; host forwards them.\n- Objects/props get deterministic ids (ID_BASE 1000000, props 2000000) so hub clients agree.\n- Next: src/view (models, clips, zonebuild, actors, vfx), src/ui (ui, glyphs, hud, menus), src/input, src/audio, src/modes (game, shell, play), src/net, tests, tools.\n- Boss HP needs tuning up (bot kills Bursar in 20-60 s; want 60-180; Malison want 120-300). Sexton single-target DPS looks low. Tune in M9 with tools/report.mjs.\nEOF\ngrep -n \"dissolve\" API.md | head -12 | cut -c1-240; sed -n 1192,1203p API.md | cut -c1-300; sed -n 1368,1387p API.md | cut -c1-260; grep -n \"rayAt\\|setZoom\\|class OrthoRig\" API.md | head -10 | cut -c1-240; sed -n 577,604p API.md | cut -c1-240; grep -n \"^### class Precipitation\" -A14 API.md | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"^### class WaterSurface\" -A12 API.md | cut -c1-200; grep -n '^### interface WaterOptions' -A12 API.md | cut -c1-180;  sed -n 3634,3700p API.md | grep -n '`' | cut -c1-200 | head -30","description":"Save progress, read materials, camera and water API"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1914,"cache_read_input_tokens":463194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1914},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"5ba39a6b-1830-4ba6-b974-5a709c74f97b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:02:09.055Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkh8mhSqpFiLY7yJhoNZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S6iNThBvXWjsTVa5PnpCud":{"command":"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Status log\n- M0 done. Sim core written (src/sim/*, src/data/*): world/hero/effects/monsters/bosses/quests/knell/round/commands/bot/zonegen. Bot finishes the campaign in the sim for all 3 classes (`node .scratch/campaign.mjs <class>`), about 10 sim minutes, level 18-19.\n- tests/ISSUES.md gets one line per issue a test catches (needed for exit interview counts).\n\n## Architecture notes (for after compaction)\n- src/sim is plain JS, reads only Rng/NavGrid from the engine. stepWorld(w, intents[seat]). All menu actions go through applyCommand(w, seat, {c:..}) in sim/commands.js.\n- Sim emits events in w.events (t: spawn, hit, death, cast, mcast, fx, lob, shot, shotx, area, areax, tele, telex, wave, zone, quest, toast, sub, talk, open, cut, boss, drop, dropx, pick, level, ...). View consumes them; host forwards them.\n- Objects/props get deterministic ids (ID_BASE 1000000, props 2000000) so hub clients agree.\n- Next: src/view (models, clips, zonebuild, actors, vfx), src/ui (ui, glyphs, hud, menus), src/input, src/audio, src/modes (game, shell, play), src/net, tests, tools.\n- Boss HP needs tuning up (bot kills Bursar in 20-60 s; want 60-180; Malison want 120-300). Sexton single-target DPS looks low. Tune in M9 with tools/report.mjs.\nEOF\ngrep -n \"dissolve\" API.md | head -12 | cut -c1-240; sed -n 1192,1203p API.md | cut -c1-300; sed -n 1368,1387p API.md | cut -c1-260; grep -n \"rayAt\\|setZoom\\|class OrthoRig\" API.md | head -10 | cut -c1-240; sed -n 577,604p API.md | cut -c1-240; grep -n \"^### class Precipitation\" -A14 API.md | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"^### class WaterSurface\" -A12 API.md | cut -c1-200; grep -n '^### interface WaterOptions' -A12 API.md | cut -c1-180;  sed -n 3634,3700p API.md | grep -n '`' | cut -c1-200 | head -30","description":"Save progress, read materials, camera and water API"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S6iNThBvXWjsTVa5PnpCud","type":"tool_result","content":"1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-\n1413:- `linger?: number`: Seconds the pieces lie around before they dissolve (default 4).\n1424:- `restore(b: Breakable): void`: Put a broken block back, whole (its old pieces dissolve as usual).\n1429:- `update(dt: number, standing = -1): void`: Per frame: tiles under `standing` (a collider handle: the character's `groundCollider`) start to shake, shaking tiles drop, dropped ones grow back; old chunks dissolve away.\n4948:const TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4951:Art pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n4956:type TransitionKind = 'fade' | 'iris' | 'diamonds' | 'dissolve' | 'dither' | 'blinds' | 'wipe' | 'curtain' | 'mosaic'\n### glowMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction glowMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n```\n\nUnlit, full-bright material for a colour (flames, eyes, screens, crystal cores), shared and\ncached per colour like `toonMaterial` (`userData.shared`; disposing it drops it from the\ncache). Its vertices snap with the toon materials' under the `ps1` filter, so a glowing part\nstays on its model.\n\n### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n### toonMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n```\n\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\n\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shade\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.di\n\n## 5. Physics\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit di\n595:- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n655:### class OrthoRig\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), an\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direct\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### interface CameraRigState\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4591-\n4592-### type PrecipitationKind\n4593-\n4594-```ts\n5086:### class WaterSurface\n5087-\n5088-- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n5089-- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n5090-- `waves: Wave[]`\n5091-- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n5092-- `readonly uOpacity: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5093-- `readonly uFoamAt: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5094-- `setWaves(waves: readonly Wave[]): void`: Change the waves (up to MAX_WAVES; the CPU height follows too).\n5095-- `update(time: number, sun?: Vector3): void`: Per frame: the waves' clock (use physics time: floaters read the same), the ripples, the sun.\n5096-- `heightAt(x: number, z: number, t = this.time): number`: World height of the drawn surface at (x, z) (waves and ripples), at the last `update` time or `t`.\n5097-- `covers(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is (x, z) over this water?\n5098-- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n5073:### interface WaterOptions\n5074-\n5075-- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the surface, m.\n5076-- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the surface at rest.\n5077-- `segments?: readonly [number, number]`: Grid quads along x and z (default: one per ripple cell, or 4 per metre without ripples).\n5078-- `waves?: readonly Wave[]`\n5079-- `ripples?: RippleField | null`: A ripple field covering the same rectangle (its size and centre must match).\n5080-- `deep?: number`: Colours (hex): troughs, crests, foam.\n5081-- `shallow?: number`\n5082-- `foam?: number`\n5083-- `foamAt?: number`: Height above rest (m) where foam starts. Default: 75% of the waves' combined height (the tallest crests).\n5084-- `opacity?: number`: 1: opaque; less: see-through by a 4×4 ordered dither per art pixel.\n5085-\n3:```ts\n5:```\n9:```ts\n11:```\n13:Partners for `n` legs in two rows (left 0, 2, 4…, right 1, 3, 5…): a leg waits for the legs beside and opposite it.\n19:foot on the ground, sliding it backwards at exactly `speed` while it is in stance, then\n21:re-run `npm run anim -- check Walk`, look at the sheet.\n25:- `name: string`\n26:- `frames: number`: One full cycle (two steps), frames at 30 fps.\n27:- `speed: number`: Ground speed the cycle is authored for (m/s at playback rate 1).\n28:- `stance: number`: Fraction of the cycle each foot is on the ground. Walk ≈ 0.55–0.6, run ≈ 0.3.\n29:- `hip: number`: Mean pelvis height offset from rest (m); negative bends the knees.\n30:- `bob?: number`: Pelvis bounce amplitude (m), twice per cycle.\n31:- `low?: number`: Cycle fraction at which the pelvis is lowest (default: walk just after contact, run mid-stance).\n32:- `squash?: number`: Squash at the lowest point (e.g. 0.05 = 5 % shorter, wider).\n33:- `lift?: number`: How high the lowest point of the swinging foot clears the floor at its peak (m).\n34:- `liftPeak?: number`: Where in the swing (0..1) the foot is highest (default 0.4).\n35:- `reach?: number`: Shift the whole stride forward (m).\n36:- `swingReach?: number`: Extra forward throw of the swinging foot late in the swing, before it settles (m).\n37:- `swingDelay?: number`: Swing timing: 0 = even, + = the foot hangs back then whips forward (running).\n38:- `plant?: number`: 0..1: how much the swinging foot sweeps back to meet the ground at touchdown. At 1 it arrives moving backwards at exactly the ground speed (still, in the world), so the foot pla\n39:- `heelStrike?: number`: Toes-up angle at heel strike (deg).\n40:- `toeOff?: number`: Heel-raise angle at toe-off (deg).\n41:- `roll?: [heel: number, toe: number]`: Fraction of stance spent rolling off the heel / onto the toes.\n42:- `tiptoe?: number`: Walk on the balls of the feet: extra pitch through stance (deg), pivoting on the ball.\n43:- `swingPitch?: number`: Extra toes-down droop mid-swing (deg).\n44:- `dangle?: number`: How much the swinging foot hangs from the shin mid-swing (0..1, default 0.8).\n45:- `lean?: number`: Torso lean forward (deg) and twist of the shoulders against the legs (deg).\n46:- `twist?: number`\n47:- `sway?: number`: Side-to-side torso roll (deg).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"402ba811-0a56-4614-aae0-b0c4278b10d7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:02:09.113Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1385:- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-\n1413:- `linger?: number`: Seconds the pieces lie around before they dissolve (default 4).\n1424:- `restore(b: Breakable): void`: Put a broken block back, whole (its old pieces dissolve as usual).\n1429:- `update(dt: number, standing = -1): void`: Per frame: tiles under `standing` (a collider handle: the character's `groundCollider`) start to shake, shaking tiles drop, dropped ones grow back; old chunks dissolve away.\n4948:const TRANSITION_CELLS: { readonly diamonds: 16; readonly blinds: 12; readonly dissolve: 3; readonly mosaic: 20; }\n4951:Art pixels per diamond cell, blind band, dissolve block; the most a mosaic block grows to.\n4956:type TransitionKind = 'fade' | 'iris' | 'diamonds' | 'dissolve' | 'dither' | 'blinds' | 'wipe' | 'curtain' | 'mosaic'\n### glowMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction glowMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation): MeshBasicNodeMaterial\n```\n\nUnlit, full-bright material for a colour (flames, eyes, screens, crystal cores), shared and\ncached per colour like `toonMaterial` (`userData.shared`; disposing it drops it from the\ncache). Its vertices snap with the toon materials' under the `ps1` filter, so a glowing part\nstays on its model.\n\n### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n### toonMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\n```\n\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\n\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shade\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.di\n\n## 5. Physics\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit di\n595:- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n655:### class OrthoRig\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), an\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direct\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### interface CameraRigState\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Shar