{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CfBp4xieFBXtzVW2nuLJRU","type":"tool_result","content":"- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\n4120:### interface DecalOptions\n4121-\n4122-- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n4123-- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.\n4124-- `color?: number`: Colour (hex). Default dark.\n4125-- `life?: number`: Seconds before it starts to fade (0: forever). Default 10.\n4126-\n4127-### class Decals\n4128-\n4129-- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n4130-- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n1159:### class ContactShadow\n1160-\n1161-Classic hard-edged blob shadow that sits on the ground under a character.\n1162-Drawn as a TSL disc (step on distance from center) so it quantizes into a crisp\n1163-pixel ellipse in pixel mode. Position it with `place()` each frame.\n1164-\n1165-- `new ContactShadow(radius = 0.45)`\n1166-- `readonly radius: number`\n1167-- `place(x: number, groundY: number, z: number, height: number): void`\n1168-\n21:15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `\n3911:### applySky()\n3914:function applySky(engine: Pick<Engine, 'sun' | 'ambient' | 'scene' | 'setSunDirection'>, s: SkyState): void\n4733:### skyAt()\n4741:### interface SkyState\n4727:### interface ShockwaveOptions\n4728-\n4729-- `radius?: number`: Final radius in screen heights. Default 0.45.\n4730-- `duration?: number`: Seconds (real time). Default 0.6.\n4731-- `strength?: number`: Push strength (1 = a strong blast). Default 1.\n4732-\n4733-### skyAt()\n2670:### interface BurstOptions\n2671-\n2672-- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n2673-- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n2674-- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n2675-- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n2676-- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n2677-\n2678-### class ParticlePool\n2679-\n2680-Fixed-size particle storage with CPU simulation. Alive particles are packed at the\n21:15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `CameraKey`, `CameraS\n22-\n23-## 1. Engine and games\n24-\n25-### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n26-\n27-```ts\n28-const ADAPTIVE_ASPECT: { readonly min: 0.4; readonly max: 2.4; }\n29-```\n30-\n31-Art aspect ratios (width / height) the adaptive mode allows; beyond them it letterboxes.\n--\n4582:- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n### interface HeadlessOptions\n\n`Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs.\n\n- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\n- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n\n### class LoadingScreen\n### buildModel()\n\n```ts\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n```\n\n### class Catalog\n\n- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\n- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\n- `has(id: string): boolean`\n- `get(id: string): T`\n- `all(): T[]`\n- `find(q: { tags?: readonly string[]; text?: string } = {}): T[]`: Defs with every tag in `tags` whose id, about or tags contain every word of `text`.\n- `search(text: string, o: SearchOptions = {}): T[]`: Defs ranked by how well they match `text`, best first (`searchDefs`).\n\n### interface CatalogEntry\n\nDefs by id: the engine's built-in libraries (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and a game's\nown. Ids are how parts, layers and saves refer to defs, so an id names one def per catalog.\n\n- `readonly id: string`\n- `readonly about: string`\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\n\n1302:### mergeStaticMeshes()\n1303-\n1304-```ts\n1305-function mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n1306-```\n1307-\n1308-Merge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\n1309-materials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\n1310-groups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n1311-\n1312-World transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\n1313-groups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n1314-`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\n1315-sources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\n1316-one collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\n1317-on screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves…\n1318-\n1249:### class LightPool\n1250-\n1251-A fixed pool of point lights shared by many requests (see the file comment). Available\n1252-to games as `ctx.lights` (sized by quality: low 4, medium 8, high 16), or create your\n1253-own with `new LightPool({ size, parent: scene })` and call `update` every frame.\n1254-\n1255-- `new LightPool(options: LightPoolOptions = {})`\n1256-- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`\n1257-- `readonly lights: PointLight[]`\n1258-- `get size: number`: Number of real lights (constant unless `resize`d).\n1259-- `request(options: LightRequestOptions = {}): LightHandle`: Ask for a light. Returns a handle to move, recolour or release.\n1260-- `update(dt: number, focus: Vector3, range = 18): void`: Assign lights for this frame. `focus` is what the camera looks at; requests further than `range` + their radius from it are not lit. Call\n1261-- `clear(): void`: Release every request at once and darken the lights (level unload).\n1262-- `resize(size: number): void`: Change the number of real lights. Every material using lights recompiles once, so do it rarely (a quality change), never per frame.\n1263-- `stats(): LightPoolStats`\n1264-- `describe(): { id: number; name: string; score: number; slot: number; level: number; alive: boolean }[]`: Every live request with its score and slot (debugging, inspectors).\n1265-- `dispose(): void`\n1266-\n1267:### interface LightPoolOptions\n1268-\n1269-- `size?: number`: Real lights in the pool (constant: changing it recompiles materials). Default 8.\n1270-- `parent?: Object3D`: Parent for the pool's lights (added to it). Usually the scene.\n1271-\n1272:### interface LightPoolStats\n122:### disposeObject()\n123-\n124-```ts\n125-function disposeObject(root: Object3D): void\n126-```\n127-\n128-Free the GPU resources of `root` and its children: geometry, materials, the textures\n129-they reference (as properties such as `map`, or inside TSL node graphs such as\n130-`colorNode = texture(t)`), and skinned meshes' bone textures.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"d986fab2-cb66-40f9-8f58-2ad3c6941e7c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:08:14.118Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel 