{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLVvsTjQfWBk2Rws6aMPDr","type":"tool_result","content":"SONG ledger song: pattern \"c\" track \"bass\" has 64 steps, expected 80\nsfx 141 songs 12 bad 1\n460:### class Settings\n461-\n462-`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463-sets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464-saved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465-settings panel.\n466-\n467-- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468-- `readonly key: string | null`\n469-- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470-- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471-- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472-- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n473-- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n474-- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n475-- `open(): void`\n476-- `close(): void`\n477-- `toggle(): void`\n478-\n--\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n493-\n494-The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495-⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496-settings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497-pressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498-\n499-- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500-- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501-- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`\n502-- `show(): void`: Show the panel with the engine's current values. The panel takes the focus, not a control: a game key pressed out of habit (D, Space) must not pick an option; Tab reaches the controls.\n503-- `hide(): void`\n504-- `sync(): void`: Put the engine's current values into the controls, and into the debug panel (the loop fills it only while the game runs).\n505-- `dispose(): void`\n506-\n507-### storeSettings()\n508-\n509-```ts\n510-function storeSettings(key: string, settings: PlayerSettings): void\n### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### QUALITY\n13:7. Input and touch: `applyDeadzone`, `ButtonEvent`, `DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS`, `GAMEPAD_BUTTONS`, `GamepadLike`, `Input`, `InputFrame`, `InputState`, `MOUSE_BUTTONS`, `PRESS_WINDOW`, `TOUCH_KEY`, `To\n14-8. Audio: `attenuation`, `AudioManager`, `AudioSettings`, `Instrument`, `Listener`, `muffleCutoff`, `noteFrequency`, `parseSong`, `PLAYGROUND_SONG`, `PlayOptions`, `renderSound`, `SFX`, `SfxName`, \n15-9. Particles: `BurstOptions`, `ParticlePool`, `ParticlePreset`, `ParticlePresetName`, `Particles`, `PARTICLES`\n16-10. HUD: `Hud`, `HudAnchor`, `HudColor`, `HudOptions`, `hudPlace`\n17-11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md): `addModelColliders`, `around`, `assetProgress`, `AssetReader`, `BakedTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `boxFrame`, `buildModel`, `Catalog`, `CatalogEntry`, `checkModel`,\n18-12. Animation toolkit: `analyzeClip`, `ClipDef`, `ClipReport`, `compileClip`, `compileClips`, `Foot`, `FootGoal`, `gaitClip`, `gaitPartners`, `GaitSpec`, `Key`, `LegDef`, `LegStepper`, `LegStepperO\n--\n2268:### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n2269-\n2270-```ts\n2271:const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n2272-```\n2273-\n2274-Standard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\n1072:- `onRecovered: ((canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) => void) | null`: Called after a lost device was recovered with a new renderer and canvas.\n2073:- `drag: number`: How hard the wind pushes. Cloth: acceleration per (m/s)² of wind hitting it squarely (light cloth: high; canvas: low). Ropes: per m/s of speed relative to the wind.\n2339:- `send(command: unknown): void`: Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked, a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straig\n2778:- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n4362:- `onRecovered: ((canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) => void) | null`: Called after a lost device was recovered with a new renderer and canvas.\n5054:- `onRecovered: ((canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) => void) | null`: Called after a lost device was recovered with a new renderer and canvas.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"6610597f-35cc-4c64-82c6-de596384d073","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:18:10.281Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"SONG ledger song: pattern \"c\" track \"bass\" has 64 steps, expected 80\nsfx 141 songs 12 bad 1\n460:### class Settings\n461-\n462-`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463-sets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464-saved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465-settings panel.\n466-\n467-- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468-- `readonly key: string | null`\n469-- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470-- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471-- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472-- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n473-- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n474-- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n475-- `open(): void`\n476-- `close(): void`\n477-- `toggle(): void`\n478-\n--\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n493-\n494-The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495-⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496-settings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497-pressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498-\n499-- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500-- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501-- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`\n502-- `show(): void`: Show the panel with the engine's current values. The panel takes the focus, not a control: a game key pressed out of habit