{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgko6s1Zv2XbR2EX84UdK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bsvamqu4hSne4XVxoSmoum","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"^### analyzeClip\" -A6 API.md | cut -c1-220; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/view/zonebuild.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    this.buildPhysics();\n    this.buildAtmosphere(biome);\n  }\"\"\",\"\"\"    this.dressPlace(biome);\n    this.buildPhysics();\n    this.buildAtmosphere(biome);\n  }\n\n  /** Authored places get their furniture. */\n  dressPlace(biome) {\n    const z = this.zone;\n    if (z.id === 'town') {\n      const ps = z.pillars;\n      if (ps.length) {\n        const cx = ps.reduce((a, p) => a + p.x, 0) / ps.length, cz = ps.reduce((a, p) => a + p.z, 0) / ps.length;\n        this.place('fountain', cx, cz, { scale: 1.2 });\n        this.lights.push(this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [cx + 1, 2.4, cz + 1], color: 0xffc080, intensity: 9, radius: 12, priority: 2 }));\n      }\n      const near = (key, dx, dz, id, o = {}) => { const n = this.view.w.objects.find((q) => q.key === key); if (n) this.place(id, n.x + dx, n.z + dz, o); };\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', -1.8, -1.6, 'market-stall', { rotY: Math.PI / 4 });\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', 2.2, -1.2, 'crate-stack', {});\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', -3.4, 0.6, 'barrel', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', -1.2, -1.8, 'anvil', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', -2.8, -0.4, 'fireplace', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', 1.6, -2, 'crate-stack', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', -1, -1.8, 'altar', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', 1.4, -1.6, 'candles', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', -2.6, -0.2, 'bookshelf', { rotY: Math.PI / 2 });\n      near('knell_font', 2.4, -1.4, 'obelisk', {});\n      near('stash', 1.8, 0.2, 'crate', {});\n      near('writ_board', -2.2, -0.6, 'bench', {});\n      near('lychgate', -2.6, 1, 'well', {});\n      near('npc_crier', 2.4, -0.8, 'statue', {});\n      near('road_gate', 0, -2.4, 'signpost', {});\n      for (const p of [[20, 4], [41, 4], [20, 21], [41, 21]]) this.place('oak', p[0], p[1], { seed: p[0], params: { h: 3 } });\n    }\n    if (z.id === 'belfry' && z.floor === 3) {\n      for (const p of z.pillars) {\n        this.lights.push(this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [p.x + 0.8, 2.6, p.z + 0.8], color: biome.torch, intensity: 9, radius: 11, flicker: 'pulse', priority: 1 }));\n        this.place('standing-torch', p.x + 1, p.z + 1, { light: false });\n      }\n    }\n    if (z.id === 'yard') {\n      const c = { x: z.entryX, z: z.entryZ };\n      this.place('coffin', c.x - 1.1, c.z - 1.1, { rotY: 0.5 });\n      this.place('tombstone', c.x - 2.2, c.z + 1.4, {});\n      this.place('tombstone', c.x + 1.6, c.z - 2.8, { seed: 2 });\n    }\n  }\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/view/view.js'; s=open(p).read()\n# tall-prop fade + footsteps + hurt sounds\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    for (const r of this.props.values()) if (r.obj.rotation.z > 0) r.obj.rotation.z = Math.max(0, r.obj.rotation.z - dt);\"\"\",\"\"\"    for (const r of this.props.values()) if (r.obj.rotation.z > 0) r.obj.rotation.z = Math.max(0, r.obj.rotation.z - dt);\n    this.updateFade(dt);\n    this.footsteps(dt);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  syncList(list, dt) {\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** Tall things between the camera and a hero go see-through, one body at a time. */\n  updateFade() {\n    this.fadeTick = (this.fadeTick ?? 0) + 1;\n    if (this.fadeTick % 6) return;\n    const heroes = this.w.heroes.filter((h) => !h.gone && !h.companion);\n    for (const r of this.objects.values()) {\n      if (!TALL_KINDS.has(r.o.kind) || !r.model || r.o.hidden) continue;\n      // The camera sits toward +X +Z: a prop hides what stands just behind it, on the -X -Z side.\n      const hide = heroes.some((h) => { const dx = r.o.x - h.x, dz = r.o.z - h.z; const along = (dx + dz) * 0.71, across = Math.abs(dx - dz) * 0.71; return along > 0 && along < 4 && across < 2; });\n      if (hide === !!r.faded) continue;\n      r.faded = hide;\n      if (hide && !r.fadeMats) {\n        r.fadeMats = [];\n        r.model.traverse((m) => {\n          if (!m.isMesh) return;\n          const c = m.material?.color;\n          if (!c || m.material.isMeshBasicNodeMaterial) { m.userData.isGlow = true; return; }\n          const clone = toonMaterial(c.getHex(), { dissolve: true }).clone();\n          clone.dissolve = 0;\n          m.userData.orig = m.material;\n          m.userData.faded = clone;\n          r.fadeMats.push(clone);\n        });\n      }\n      r.model.traverse((m) => {\n        if (!m.isMesh) return;\n        if (m.userData.isGlow) { m.visible = !hide; return; }\n        if (m.userData.faded) { m.material = hide ? m.userData.faded : m.userData.orig; if (hide) m.material.dissolve = 0.6; }\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  footsteps(dt) {\n    const h = this.game.localHero?.();\n    if (!h || !h.moving || h.dead) return;\n    this.stepT = (this.stepT ?? 0) - dt;\n    if (this.stepT > 0) return;\n    this.stepT = 0.3;\n    const b = this.w.zone?.biome;\n    const name = b === 'yard' || b === 'causeway' || b === 'pantry' ? 'step_mud' : b === 'town' ? 'step_wood' : 'step_stone';\n    this.sfx(name, { x: h.x, z: h.z });\n  }\n\n  syncList(list, dt) {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      const voice = MAT_SOUND[a.def.mat] ?? 'hit_flesh';\n      this.sfx(voice, { x: e.x, z: e.z, n: e.c ? 2 : 0 });\"\"\",\"\"\"      const voice = MAT_SOUND[a.def.mat] ?? 'hit_flesh';\n      this.sfx(voice, { x: e.x, z: e.z, n: e.c ? 2 : 0 });\n      if (a.def.voice && this.fxRng.chance(0.25)) this.sfx('mon_hurt', { x: e.x, z: e.z, v: a.def.voice });\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (!e.companion && !this.game.isSession) { this.ctx.engine.timeScale = Math.min(this.ctx.engine.timeScale, 0.25); this.slowT = 0.8; }\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (!e.companion && !this.game.isSession && this.game.humanCount() <= 1) { this.ctx.engine.timeScale = Math.min(this.ctx.engine.timeScale, 0.25); this.slowT = 0.8; }\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"const PROP_COLORS = {\"\"\",\"\"\"const TALL_KINDS = new Set(['lychgate', 'gibbet', 'gate', 'wagon', 'font', 'board']);\nconst PROP_COLORS = {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"import { buildModel, Decals, disposeObject, glowMaterial, PALETTE, Rng, setLookLayer, THREE, Trail } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\",\"import { buildModel, Decals, disposeObject, glowMaterial, PALETTE, Rng, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, Trail } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/audio/audio.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (name === 'mon_attack' || name === 'mon_wake' || name === 'mon_death') {\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (name === 'mon_attack' || name === 'mon_wake' || name === 'mon_death' || name === 'mon_hurt') {\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/sim/knell.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  ev(w, { t: 'run_floor', floor: w.zone.floor });\n  if (w.camp && !w.camp.plateRun && w.rng.chance(1 / 3)) { w.plateAt = w.time + w.rng.range(20, 60); w.camp.plateRun = true; }\"\"\",\"\"\"  ev(w, { t: 'run_floor', floor: w.zone.floor });\n  if (w.zone.floor === 0 && !w.round && w.rng.chance(1 / 3)) w.plateAt = w.time + w.rng.range(20, 60);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    ev(w, { t: 'warden', k: r.wardenType, x: p.x, z: p.z });\n    telegraphRing(w, p.x, p.z, 3, 0.6, 0, {});\"\"\",\"\"\"    ev(w, { t: 'warden', k: r.wardenType, x: p.x, z: p.z });\n    telegraphRing(w, p.x, p.z, 3, 0.6, 0, {});\n    boneRing(w, p.x, p.z, 10);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"export function endRun(w) { w.run = null; }\"\"\",\"\"\"/** A broken ring of bone around the Warden: every third cell stays open, so nobody is shut out. */\nfunction boneRing(w, x, z, R) {\n  const cells = [];\n  const cx = Math.floor(x), cz = Math.floor(z);\n  for (let i = -R; i <= R; i++) {\n    for (let j = -R; j <= R; j++) {\n      const d = Math.hypot(i, j);\n      if (d < R - 0.5 || d > R + 0.5 || (i + j + 300) % 3 === 0) continue;\n      const col = cx + i, row = cz + j;\n      if (!w.zone.nav.isOpen(col, row) || w.heroes.some((h) => Math.floor(h.x) === col && Math.floor(h.z) === row)) continue;\n      cells.push([col, row]);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const [col, row] of cells) setCellOpen(w, col, row, false);\n  const o = { id: nextId(w), x, z, cells, life: 90, kind: 'bone_wall' };\n  w.obstacles.push(o);\n  ev(w, { t: 'obst', id: o.id, k: 'bone_wall', x, z, cells, life: 90 });\n}\n\nexport function endRun(w) { w.run = null; }\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"import { dist, ev, say, toast } from './core.js';\",\"import { dist, ev, nextId, say, setCellOpen, toast } from './core.js';\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/ui/hud.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (hovered?.def?.boss) void 0;\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (w.round && w.round.playT < 30) {\n      for (const o of w.objects) {\n        if (o.kind !== 'class_font') continue;\n        const [sx, sy] = view.project(o.x, 1.4, o.z);\n        ui.text(sx, sy, o.label, { color: CLASSES[o.cls].color, align: 'center' });\n      }\n    }\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/modes/game.js'; s=open(p).read()\n# opening get-up, credits, wheel zoom, couch teleport\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      this.openScreen(new Cutscene(this, { ...STORY.opening() }));\"\"\",\"\"\"      this.openScreen(new Cutscene(this, { ...STORY.opening({ onEnd: () => this.coffinBurst() }) }));\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  leaveShell() {\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** Your coffin bursts and you get up: it did not take. */\n  coffinBurst() {\n    const h = this.world?.heroes[0];\n    const a = h && this.view.actors.get(h.id);\n    if (!a) return;\n    a.play('GetUp', 1, false);\n    this.view.fx.shatter(h.x, 0.05, h.z, PALETTE.plum, h.x, h.z, this.uiRng, { count: 16, size: 0.3, spread: 0.7, speed: 6 });\n    this.view.showFx({ k: 'dust_ring', s: 'coffin_slam', sh: 0.4, x: h.x, z: h.z, r: 3 });\n    this.audioSys.zoneChanged(this.world.zone);\n  }\n\n  leaveShell() {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      onEnd: () => {\n        ctx.engine.screen.flash('white', { duration: 0.6 });\n        this.persist();\n        if (first) {\n          import('../ui/menus/pause.js').then(() => {});\n          this.hudSys.toast('PENANCE AND KNELL RUNS ARE OPEN AT THE FONT', 'sand', { big: true, life: 6 });\n        }\n        this.cmd({ c: 'dev_goto', zone: 'town', floor: 0 });\n      },\"\"\",\"\"\"      onEnd: () => {\n        ctx.engine.screen.flash('white', { duration: 0.6 });\n        this.persist();\n        const home = () => {\n          if (first) this.hudSys.toast('PENANCE AND KNELL RUNS ARE OPEN AT THE FONT', 'sand', { big: true, life: 6 });\n          this.cmd({ c: 'dev_goto', zone: 'town', floor: 0 });\n        };\n        if (first && !this.skipCutscenes) this.openScreen(new CreditsRoll(this, home));\n        else home();\n      },\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"import { AboutScreen, HowToScreen, LOOKS, PartyScreen, PauseScreen, SettingsScreen } from '../ui/menus/pause.js';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { AboutScreen, CreditsRoll, HowToScreen, LOOKS, PartyScreen, PauseScreen, SettingsScreen } from '../ui/menus/pause.js';\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"import { Rng, THREE, LOOK_PRESETS, MODEL_LIBRARY } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { LOOK_PRESETS, MODEL_LIBRARY, PALETTE, Rng, THREE } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    this.labelsHeld = false;\n    const seats = this.localSeats();\"\"\",\"\"\"    this.labelsHeld = false;\n    const seats = this.localSeats();\n    if (this.input.wheelNow && !top) {\n      this.settings.zoom = Math.max(0.6, Math.min(1.4, Math.round((this.settings.zoom - this.input.wheelNow * 0.1) * 100) / 100));\n    }\n    this.couchLeash(real);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  playFrame() {\n    const w = this.world;\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** One camera: a hero off screen for two seconds comes back to seat one. */\n  couchLeash() {\n    const w = this.world;\n    if (this.isSession || w.heroes.filter((h) => !h.companion && !h.gone).length < 2) return;\n    const lead = w.heroes.find((h) => h.seat === 0);\n    const hud = this.ctx.hud;\n    for (const h of w.heroes) {\n      if (h === lead || h.gone || h.companion || h.dead) continue;\n      const [x, y] = this.view.project(h.x, 1, h.z);\n      const off = x < -4 || y < -4 || x > hud.width + 4 || y > hud.height + 4;\n      h.offT = off ? (h.offT ?? 0) + this.lastRealDt : 0;\n      if (h.offT > 2) { h.offT = 0; h.x = lead.x; h.z = lead.z; this.view.showFx({ k: 'portal', s: 'blink', x: h.x, z: h.z, r: 1.5 }); }\n    }\n  }\n\n  playFrame() {\n    const w = this.world;\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"    const real = this.realDt(ctx, dt);\\n    this.lastRealDt = real;\",\"    const real = this.realDt(ctx, dt);\\n    this.lastRealDt = real;\")\ns=s.replace(\"    this.couchLeash(real);\",\"    this.couchLeash();\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/ui/menus/pause.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"// ---- About ------\"\"\",\"\"\"/** The last thing the story shows: who did it, and the deeper bell. */\nexport class CreditsRoll extends Screen {\n  constructor(game, onDone) {\n    super(game, { tag: 'credits', freeze: false, holdSim: true, covers: true });\n    this.onDone = onDone;\n    this.y = 0;\n    this.lines = [\n      [TITLE, 'sand', 3], ['', 'white', 1], ['THE GREAT BELL RANG TRUE', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['CRIER MAUDLIN, A HEAD', 'sand', 1], ['DAME BRASSE, RATHER LOUD', 'orange', 1], ['MOTHER OGIVE, BY TASTE', 'lime', 1], ['PENNYWHISTLE, AT A MODEST MARKUP', 'sky', 1], ['SISTER PYX, AND THE CROSSBOW', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['BISHOP AMBROSE, THRICE BURIED', 'mist', 1], ['THE BURSAR, IN ARREARS', 'red', 1], ['MALISON, THE UNRUNG SAINT', 'red', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['EVERY MODEL, CLIP, SONG, SOUND AND VOICE', 'white', 1], ['IS DATA IN THE SOURCE', 'white', 1], ['BUILT ON THE PIXEL ENGINE KIT', 'mist', 1], ['THE FULL CREDITS ARE ON THE ABOUT SCREEN', 'mist', 1], ['', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['AND FAR BELOW, UNDER THE FOUNDATION, UNDER THE SAINT', 'mist', 1], ['A MUCH DEEPER BELL ANSWERED', 'sand', 1], ['', 'white', 1], ['KNELL RUNS AND PENANCE ARE OPEN', 'lime', 1],\n    ];\n  }\n  back() { this.finish(); }\n  finish() { if (this.done) return; this.done = true; this.game.closeScreen(); this.onDone?.(); }\n  draw(ui) {\n    const g = this.game;\n    this.y += g.lastRealDt * 16;\n    ui.rect(0, 0, ui.w, ui.h, 'ink');\n    let y = ui.h - this.y;\n    for (const [t, c, sc] of this.lines) {\n      if (t && y > -30 && y < ui.h - 20) ui.text(ui.w / 2, y, t, { color: c, scale: sc, align: 'center' });\n      y += 12 * sc + 2;\n    }\n    if (!this.toll && y < ui.h * 0.5) { this.toll = true; g.audioSys?.sfx('bell_true', { pitch: -7 }); }\n    if (y < 0) this.finish();\n    if (g.input.menu.confirm || g.input.menu.click) this.y += 60;\n    ui.prompt('confirm', 'FASTER', 14, ui.h - 14);\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- About ------\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tests/browser/all.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"test('the kit agrees:\"\"\",\"\"\"test('a save round-trips through a reload, and Continue picks it up', async () => {\n  const { context, page, errors } = await freshPage();\n  await step(page, 3);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await skipOpening(page);\n  const before = await ev(page, () => { const g = window.__GAME__; g.cmd({ c: 'dev_level', n: 4 }); g.cmd({ c: 'dev_gold', n: 777 }); g.cmd({ c: 'dev_item', slot: 'ring', rarity: 'reliquary' }); g.world.camp.flags.pyx = 1; g.persist(); const h = g.world.heroes[0]; return { level: h.level, gold: h.gold, item: h.inv.find(Boolean).name, name: h.name, q: g.world.camp.q.s }; });\n  await page.reload();\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__PIXEL_READY__, null, { timeout: 60000 });\n  await page.evaluate(() => window.__PIXEL_READY__);\n  await ev(page, () => { window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__.manual = true; });\n  await step(page, 3);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  eq(await top(page), 'menu', 'menu after the reload');\n  assert((await texts(page)).includes('CONTINUE'), 'Continue offered');\n  eq(await focus(page), 'menu:CONTINUE', 'focus starts on Continue');\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  eq(await top(page), 'heroselect', 'hero select');\n  assert((await texts(page)).includes(before.name), 'my hero is listed');\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 3);\n  const after = await ev(page, () => { const g = window.__GAME__; const h = g.world.heroes[0]; return { level: h.level, gold: h.gold, item: h.inv.find(Boolean)?.name, name: h.name, q: g.world.camp.q.s, mode: g.mode }; });\n  eq(after.mode, 'play', 'in play');\n  eq(after.level, before.level, 'level kept');\n  eq(after.gold, before.gold, 'gold kept');\n  eq(after.item, before.item, 'item kept');\n  eq(after.name, before.name, 'name kept');\n  // Music stays where the player left it, and the flag is ours.\n  assert(!errors.length, errors[0]);\n  await context.close();\n});\n\ntest('WebKit here has no WebGPU: it shows the no-WebGPU page', async () => {\n  const { webkit } = await import('playwright');\n  const browser = await webkit.launch();\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\n  await page.goto(`file://${HTML}`);\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('WebGPU') || window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__, null, { timeout: 30000 });\n  const t = await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText);\n  const hasGpu = await page.evaluate(() => !!navigator.gpu);\n  if (!hasGpu) { assert(t.includes('needs WebGPU'), `page says: ${t.slice(0, 200)}`); assert(t.includes('Diabellical'), 'title on the page'); }\n  await browser.close();\n});\n\ntest('the kit agrees:\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > docs/DESIGNERS.md <<'EOF'\n# Building the rest of the game\n\nEverything a designer touches is plain data in `src/data`, rooms are ASCII, models are `ModelDef`s, songs\nare text patterns. Dev mode (pause menu) tests any of it at once. Run `node tools/build.mjs` then open the\nHTML, and `node tools/test.mjs --sim` tells you if the data refers to something that does not exist.\n\n## Add a monster\n1. Add a row to `MONSTERS` in `src/data/monsters.js`: `hp` and `hit` multiply the level formulas, `ai` names a\n   state machine in `src/sim/monsters.js` (`melee lunge leaper ranged slam bomber hook blinker charger swooper necro plate spawner`).\n2. Add a body to `src/view/models/monsters.js`. Humanoids use `humanoid({...})` and get all hero clips.\n   `node check.mjs --sheets src/view/models/monsters.js` draws it.\n3. Add it to a zone's `monsters` table in `src/data/zones.js`, with a weight.\n4. Dev mode, SPAWN tab, to meet it. Its Bestiary entry appears by itself.\n\n## Add a skill or a Tone\nAdd to `SKILLS` in `src/data/skills.js`. `fx` is a list of ops, and the ops are the whole vocabulary:\n`arc circle cone ring projectile lob chain dash leap blink zone obstacle summon turret buff debuff pull knock\nstun apply_status consume_status consume_graves comet_rain delay repeat spawn_decoy`. A Tone has `patch` (fields\non the skill), `fx` (overrides per op index) and `add` (more ops). Add the id to the class in `src/data/classes.js`.\n\n## Add an item, a legendary, a set, an affix\n`src/data/items.js`. A legendary needs a row in `LEGENDARIES` and a hook object of the same id in\n`src/sim/powers.js`: `onCast`, `onHit`, `onKill`, `onPickup`, `tick`, `modifySkill`.\n\n## Add a room\nAdd an ASCII template to `src/data/rooms/`: `#` wall, `.` floor, `~` water or pit, `P` pillar, `D` door socket,\n`S` trash spawn, `E` elite spawn, `C` chest, `B` breakable, `T` trap, `L` light, `A` shrine, `X` way in or on,\n`N` named prop from the template's `named` list. List it in a zone's `gen.fill`. The tests walk it for 200 seeds.\n\n## Add a zone\nAdd to `ZONES` and `BIOMES` in `src/data/zones.js`, give it a song in `ZONE_SONGS` (`src/data/songs.js`), and\nsomewhere to enter from: a named `exit`, or a line in the Map screen's list and `zoneOpen` in `src/sim/commands.js`.\n\n## Add a quest\nSteps go in `QUESTS` (`src/data/quests.js`). What ends a step goes in `src/sim/quests.js`: `onTalkDone`,\n`onObjectUsed`, `onBossKilled`, `onZoneEntered`, or `stepCheap` for positions. `objectiveOf` tells the map marker\nand the bot where to go. Lines for a step go in `TALKS` in `src/data/dialog.js`, keyed `npc:quest.step`.\n\n## Add a song or a sound\nSongs are `S('D4:4 r:4 A4:2')` strings in `src/data/songs.js`: note and length in steps, `r` is a rest. Every track of a\npattern must add up to the same length (the tests say which one does not). Sounds are `SoundDef`s in `src/data/sfx.js`.\n\n## Tune it\n`src/data/tuning.js` holds the formulas and the sliders. Every row of `TUNING` is a live slider in dev mode.\n`node tools/report.mjs 11,12` plays the campaign with the bot and prints minutes, levels, boss times and drops.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet 2>&1 | tail -n 3; timeout 100 node tools/test.mjs --sim 2>&1 | tail -n 5 | cut -c1-400;timeout 300 node tools/test.mjs --browser \"save\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-500; timeout 100 node tools/test.mjs --browser \"WebKit\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-500","description":"Apply polish batch, add save and WebKit tests, run them","timeout":520000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":851,"cache_read_input_tokens":906758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":851},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"2c8257f5-96b6-48ce-9a5a-ee090273e9fe","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:21:34.734Z","request_id":"req_011Cgko6rhiTrNco86aZ9V3n","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Bsvamqu4hSne4XVxoSmoum":{"command":"grep -n \"^### analyzeClip\" -A6 API.md | cut -c1-220; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/view/zonebuild.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    this.buildPhysics();\n    this.buildAtmosphere(biome);\n  }\"\"\",\"\"\"    this.dressPlace(biome);\n    this.buildPhysics();\n    this.buildAtmosphere(biome);\n  }\n\n  /** Authored places get their furniture. */\n  dressPlace(biome) {\n    const z = this.zone;\n    if (z.id === 'town') {\n      const ps = z.pillars;\n      if (ps.length) {\n        const cx = ps.reduce((a, p) => a + p.x, 0) / ps.length, cz = ps.reduce((a, p) => a + p.z, 0) / ps.length;\n        this.place('fountain', cx, cz, { scale: 1.2 });\n        this.lights.push(this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [cx + 1, 2.4, cz + 1], color: 0xffc080, intensity: 9, radius: 12, priority: 2 }));\n      }\n      const near = (key, dx, dz, id, o = {}) => { const n = this.view.w.objects.find((q) => q.key === key); if (n) this.place(id, n.x + dx, n.z + dz, o); };\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', -1.8, -1.6, 'market-stall', { rotY: Math.PI / 4 });\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', 2.2, -1.2, 'crate-stack', {});\n      near('npc_pennywhistle', -3.4, 0.6, 'barrel', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', -1.2, -1.8, 'anvil', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', -2.8, -0.4, 'fireplace', {});\n      near('npc_brasse', 1.6, -2, 'crate-stack', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', -1, -1.8, 'altar', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', 1.4, -1.6, 'candles', {});\n      near('npc_ogive', -2.6, -0.2, 'bookshelf', { rotY: Math.PI / 2 });\n      near('knell_font', 2.4, -1.4, 'obelisk', {});\n      near('stash', 1.8, 0.2, 'crate', {});\n      near('writ_board', -2.2, -0.6, 'bench', {});\n      near('lychgate', -2.6, 1, 'well', {});\n      near('npc_crier', 2.4, -0.8, 'statue', {});\n      near('road_gate', 0, -2.4, 'signpost', {});\n      for (const p of [[20, 4], [41, 4], [20, 21], [41, 21]]) this.place('oak', p[0], p[1], { seed: p[0], params: { h: 3 } });\n    }\n    if (z.id === 'belfry' && z.floor === 3) {\n      for (const p of z.pillars) {\n        this.lights.push(this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [p.x + 0.8, 2.6, p.z + 0.8], color: biome.torch, intensity: 9, radius: 11, flicker: 'pulse', priority: 1 }));\n        this.place('standing-torch', p.x + 1, p.z + 1, { light: false });\n      }\n    }\n    if (z.id === 'yard') {\n      const c = { x: z.entryX, z: z.entryZ };\n      this.place('coffin', c.x - 1.1, c.z - 1.1, { rotY: 0.5 });\n      this.place('tombstone', c.x - 2.2, c.z + 1.4, {});\n      this.place('tombstone', c.x + 1.6, c.z - 2.8, { seed: 2 });\n    }\n  }\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/view/view.js'; s=open(p).read()\n# tall-prop fade + footsteps + hurt sounds\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    for (const r of this.props.values()) if (r.obj.rotation.z > 0) r.obj.rotation.z = Math.max(0, r.obj.rotation.z - dt);\"\"\",\"\"\"    for (const r of this.props.values()) if (r.obj.rotation.z > 0) r.obj.rotation.z = Math.max(0, r.obj.rotation.z - dt);\n    this.updateFade(dt);\n    this.footsteps(dt);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  syncList(list, dt) {\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** Tall things between the camera and a hero go see-through, one body at a time. */\n  updateFade() {\n    this.fadeTick = (this.fadeTick ?? 0) + 1;\n    if (this.fadeTick % 6) return;\n    const heroes = this.w.heroes.filter((h) => !h.gone && !h.companion);\n    for (const r of this.objects.values()) {\n      if (!TALL_KINDS.has(r.o.kind) || !r.model || r.o.hidden) continue;\n      // The camera sits toward +X +Z: a prop hides what stands just behind it, on the -X -Z side.\n      const hide = heroes.some((h) => { const dx = r.o.x - h.x, dz = r.o.z - h.z; const along = (dx + dz) * 0.71, across = Math.abs(dx - dz) * 0.71; return along > 0 && along < 4 && across < 2; });\n      if (hide === !!r.faded) continue;\n      r.faded = hide;\n      if (hide && !r.fadeMats) {\n        r.fadeMats = [];\n        r.model.traverse((m) => {\n          if (!m.isMesh) return;\n          const c = m.material?.color;\n          if (!c || m.material.isMeshBasicNodeMaterial) { m.userData.isGlow = true; return; }\n          const clone = toonMaterial(c.getHex(), { dissolve: true }).clone();\n          clone.dissolve = 0;\n          m.userData.orig = m.material;\n          m.userData.faded = clone;\n          r.fadeMats.push(clone);\n        });\n      }\n      r.model.traverse((m) => {\n        if (!m.isMesh) return;\n        if (m.userData.isGlow) { m.visible = !hide; return; }\n        if (m.userData.faded) { m.material = hide ? m.userData.faded : m.userData.orig; if (hide) m.material.dissolve = 0.6; }\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  footsteps(dt) {\n    const h = this.game.localHero?.();\n    if (!h || !h.moving || h.dead) return;\n    this.stepT = (this.stepT ?? 0) - dt;\n    if (this.stepT > 0) return;\n    this.stepT = 0.3;\n    const b = this.w.zone?.biome;\n    const name = b === 'yard' || b === 'causeway' || b === 'pantry' ? 'step_mud' : b === 'town' ? 'step_wood' : 'step_stone';\n    this.sfx(name, { x: h.x, z: h.z });\n  }\n\n  syncList(list, dt) {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      const voice = MAT_SOUND[a.def.mat] ?? 'hit_flesh';\n      this.sfx(voice, { x: e.x, z: e.z, n: e.c ? 2 : 0 });\"\"\",\"\"\"      const voice = MAT_SOUND[a.def.mat] ?? 'hit_flesh';\n      this.sfx(voice, { x: e.x, z: e.z, n: e.c ? 2 : 0 });\n      if (a.def.voice && this.fxRng.chance(0.25)) this.sfx('mon_hurt', { x: e.x, z: e.z, v: a.def.voice });\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (!e.companion && !this.game.isSession) { this.ctx.engine.timeScale = Math.min(this.ctx.engine.timeScale, 0.25); this.slowT = 0.8; }\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (!e.companion && !this.game.isSession && this.game.humanCount() <= 1) { this.ctx.engine.timeScale = Math.min(this.ctx.engine.timeScale, 0.25); this.slowT = 0.8; }\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"const PROP_COLORS = {\"\"\",\"\"\"const TALL_KINDS = new Set(['lychgate', 'gibbet', 'gate', 'wagon', 'font', 'board']);\nconst PROP_COLORS = {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"import { buildModel, Decals, disposeObject, glowMaterial, PALETTE, Rng, setLookLayer, THREE, Trail } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\",\"import { buildModel, Decals, disposeObject, glowMaterial, PALETTE, Rng, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, Trail } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/audio/audio.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (name === 'mon_attack' || name === 'mon_wake' || name === 'mon_death') {\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (name === 'mon_attack' || name === 'mon_wake' || name === 'mon_death' || name === 'mon_hurt') {\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/sim/knell.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  ev(w, { t: 'run_floor', floor: w.zone.floor });\n  if (w.camp && !w.camp.plateRun && w.rng.chance(1 / 3)) { w.plateAt = w.time + w.rng.range(20, 60); w.camp.plateRun = true; }\"\"\",\"\"\"  ev(w, { t: 'run_floor', floor: w.zone.floor });\n  if (w.zone.floor === 0 && !w.round && w.rng.chance(1 / 3)) w.plateAt = w.time + w.rng.range(20, 60);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    ev(w, { t: 'warden', k: r.wardenType, x: p.x, z: p.z });\n    telegraphRing(w, p.x, p.z, 3, 0.6, 0, {});\"\"\",\"\"\"    ev(w, { t: 'warden', k: r.wardenType, x: p.x, z: p.z });\n    telegraphRing(w, p.x, p.z, 3, 0.6, 0, {});\n    boneRing(w, p.x, p.z, 10);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"export function endRun(w) { w.run = null; }\"\"\",\"\"\"/** A broken ring of bone around the Warden: every third cell stays open, so nobody is shut out. */\nfunction boneRing(w, x, z, R) {\n  const cells = [];\n  const cx = Math.floor(x), cz = Math.floor(z);\n  for (let i = -R; i <= R; i++) {\n    for (let j = -R; j <= R; j++) {\n      const d = Math.hypot(i, j);\n      if (d < R - 0.5 || d > R + 0.5 || (i + j + 300) % 3 === 0) continue;\n      const col = cx + i, row = cz + j;\n      if (!w.zone.nav.isOpen(col, row) || w.heroes.some((h) => Math.floor(h.x) === col && Math.floor(h.z) === row)) continue;\n      cells.push([col, row]);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const [col, row] of cells) setCellOpen(w, col, row, false);\n  const o = { id: nextId(w), x, z, cells, life: 90, kind: 'bone_wall' };\n  w.obstacles.push(o);\n  ev(w, { t: 'obst', id: o.id, k: 'bone_wall', x, z, cells, life: 90 });\n}\n\nexport function endRun(w) { w.run = null; }\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"import { dist, ev, say, toast } from './core.js';\",\"import { dist, ev, nextId, say, setCellOpen, toast } from './core.js';\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/ui/hud.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    if (hovered?.def?.boss) void 0;\"\"\",\"\"\"    if (w.round && w.round.playT < 30) {\n      for (const o of w.objects) {\n        if (o.kind !== 'class_font') continue;\n        const [sx, sy] = view.project(o.x, 1.4, o.z);\n        ui.text(sx, sy, o.label, { color: CLASSES[o.cls].color, align: 'center' });\n      }\n    }\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/modes/game.js'; s=open(p).read()\n# opening get-up, credits, wheel zoom, couch teleport\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      this.openScreen(new Cutscene(this, { ...STORY.opening() }));\"\"\",\"\"\"      this.openScreen(new Cutscene(this, { ...STORY.opening({ onEnd: () => this.coffinBurst() }) }));\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  leaveShell() {\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** Your coffin bursts and you get up: it did not take. */\n  coffinBurst() {\n    const h = this.world?.heroes[0];\n    const a = h && this.view.actors.get(h.id);\n    if (!a) return;\n    a.play('GetUp', 1, false);\n    this.view.fx.shatter(h.x, 0.05, h.z, PALETTE.plum, h.x, h.z, this.uiRng, { count: 16, size: 0.3, spread: 0.7, speed: 6 });\n    this.view.showFx({ k: 'dust_ring', s: 'coffin_slam', sh: 0.4, x: h.x, z: h.z, r: 3 });\n    this.audioSys.zoneChanged(this.world.zone);\n  }\n\n  leaveShell() {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"      onEnd: () => {\n        ctx.engine.screen.flash('white', { duration: 0.6 });\n        this.persist();\n        if (first) {\n          import('../ui/menus/pause.js').then(() => {});\n          this.hudSys.toast('PENANCE AND KNELL RUNS ARE OPEN AT THE FONT', 'sand', { big: true, life: 6 });\n        }\n        this.cmd({ c: 'dev_goto', zone: 'town', floor: 0 });\n      },\"\"\",\"\"\"      onEnd: () => {\n        ctx.engine.screen.flash('white', { duration: 0.6 });\n        this.persist();\n        const home = () => {\n          if (first) this.hudSys.toast('PENANCE AND KNELL RUNS ARE OPEN AT THE FONT', 'sand', { big: true, life: 6 });\n          this.cmd({ c: 'dev_goto', zone: 'town', floor: 0 });\n        };\n        if (first && !this.skipCutscenes) this.openScreen(new CreditsRoll(this, home));\n        else home();\n      },\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"import { AboutScreen, HowToScreen, LOOKS, PartyScreen, PauseScreen, SettingsScreen } from '../ui/menus/pause.js';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { AboutScreen, CreditsRoll, HowToScreen, LOOKS, PartyScreen, PauseScreen, SettingsScreen } from '../ui/menus/pause.js';\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"import { Rng, THREE, LOOK_PRESETS, MODEL_LIBRARY } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\"\"\",\"\"\"import { LOOK_PRESETS, MODEL_LIBRARY, PALETTE, Rng, THREE } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    this.labelsHeld = false;\n    const seats = this.localSeats();\"\"\",\"\"\"    this.labelsHeld = false;\n    const seats = this.localSeats();\n    if (this.input.wheelNow && !top) {\n      this.settings.zoom = Math.max(0.6, Math.min(1.4, Math.round((this.settings.zoom - this.input.wheelNow * 0.1) * 100) / 100));\n    }\n    this.couchLeash(real);\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  playFrame() {\n    const w = this.world;\"\"\",\"\"\"  /** One camera: a hero off screen for two seconds comes back to seat one. */\n  couchLeash() {\n    const w = this.world;\n    if (this.isSession || w.heroes.filter((h) => !h.companion && !h.gone).length < 2) return;\n    const lead = w.heroes.find((h) => h.seat === 0);\n    const hud = this.ctx.hud;\n    for (const h of w.heroes) {\n      if (h === lead || h.gone || h.companion || h.dead) continue;\n      const [x, y] = this.view.project(h.x, 1, h.z);\n      const off = x < -4 || y < -4 || x > hud.width + 4 || y > hud.height + 4;\n      h.offT = off ? (h.offT ?? 0) + this.lastRealDt : 0;\n      if (h.offT > 2) { h.offT = 0; h.x = lead.x; h.z = lead.z; this.view.showFx({ k: 'portal', s: 'blink', x: h.x, z: h.z, r: 1.5 }); }\n    }\n  }\n\n  playFrame() {\n    const w = this.world;\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"    const real = this.realDt(ctx, dt);\\n    this.lastRealDt = real;\",\"    const real = this.realDt(ctx, dt);\\n    this.lastRealDt = real;\")\ns=s.replace(\"    this.couchLeash(real);\",\"    this.couchLeash();\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='src/ui/menus/pause.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"// ---- About ------\"\"\",\"\"\"/** The last thing the story shows: who did it, and the deeper bell. */\nexport class CreditsRoll extends Screen {\n  constructor(game, onDone) {\n    super(game, { tag: 'credits', freeze: false, holdSim: true, covers: true });\n    this.onDone = onDone;\n    this.y = 0;\n    this.lines = [\n      [TITLE, 'sand', 3], ['', 'white', 1], ['THE GREAT BELL RANG TRUE', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['CRIER MAUDLIN, A HEAD', 'sand', 1], ['DAME BRASSE, RATHER LOUD', 'orange', 1], ['MOTHER OGIVE, BY TASTE', 'lime', 1], ['PENNYWHISTLE, AT A MODEST MARKUP', 'sky', 1], ['SISTER PYX, AND THE CROSSBOW', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['BISHOP AMBROSE, THRICE BURIED', 'mist', 1], ['THE BURSAR, IN ARREARS', 'red', 1], ['MALISON, THE UNRUNG SAINT', 'red', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['EVERY MODEL, CLIP, SONG, SOUND AND VOICE', 'white', 1], ['IS DATA IN THE SOURCE', 'white', 1], ['BUILT ON THE PIXEL ENGINE KIT', 'mist', 1], ['THE FULL CREDITS ARE ON THE ABOUT SCREEN', 'mist', 1], ['', 'white', 1], ['', 'white', 1],\n      ['AND FAR BELOW, UNDER THE FOUNDATION, UNDER THE SAINT', 'mist', 1], ['A MUCH DEEPER BELL ANSWERED', 'sand', 1], ['', 'white', 1], ['KNELL RUNS AND PENANCE ARE OPEN', 'lime', 1],\n    ];\n  }\n  back() { this.finish(); }\n  finish() { if (this.done) return; this.done = true; this.game.closeScreen(); this.onDone?.(); }\n  draw(ui) {\n    const g = this.game;\n    this.y += g.lastRealDt * 16;\n    ui.rect(0, 0, ui.w, ui.h, 'ink');\n    let y = ui.h - this.y;\n    for (const [t, c, sc] of this.lines) {\n      if (t && y > -30 && y < ui.h - 20) ui.text(ui.w / 2, y, t, { color: c, scale: sc, align: 'center' });\n      y += 12 * sc + 2;\n    }\n    if (!this.toll && y < ui.h * 0.5) { this.toll = true; g.audioSys?.sfx('bell_true', { pitch: -7 }); }\n    if (y < 0) this.finish();\n    if (g.input.menu.confirm || g.input.menu.click) this.y += 60;\n    ui.prompt('confirm', 'FASTER', 14, ui.h - 14);\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- About ------\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tests/browser/all.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"test('the kit agrees:\"\"\",\"\"\"test('a save round-trips through a reload, and Continue picks it up', async () => {\n  const { context, page, errors } = await freshPage();\n  await step(page, 3);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  await skipOpening(page);\n  const before = await ev(page, () => { const g = window.__GAME__; g.cmd({ c: 'dev_level', n: 4 }); g.cmd({ c: 'dev_gold', n: 777 }); g.cmd({ c: 'dev_item', slot: 'ring', rarity: 'reliquary' }); g.world.camp.flags.pyx = 1; g.persist(); const h = g.world.heroes[0]; return { level: h.level, gold: h.gold, item: h.inv.find(Boolean).name, name: h.name, q: g.world.camp.q.s }; });\n  await page.reload();\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__PIXEL_READY__, null, { timeout: 60000 });\n  await page.evaluate(() => window.__PIXEL_READY__);\n  await ev(page, () => { window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__.manual = true; });\n  await step(page, 3);\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  eq(await top(page), 'menu', 'menu after the reload');\n  assert((await texts(page)).includes('CONTINUE'), 'Continue offered');\n  eq(await focus(page), 'menu:CONTINUE', 'focus starts on Continue');\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 2);\n  eq(await top(page), 'heroselect', 'hero select');\n  assert((await texts(page)).includes(before.name), 'my hero is listed');\n  await keyTap(page, 'Enter'); await step(page, 3);\n  const after = await ev(page, () => { const g = window.__GAME__; const h = g.world.heroes[0]; return { level: h.level, gold: h.gold, item: h.inv.find(Boolean)?.name, name: h.name, q: g.world.camp.q.s, mode: g.mode }; });\n  eq(after.mode, 'play', 'in play');\n  eq(after.level, before.level, 'level kept');\n  eq(after.gold, before.gold, 'gold kept');\n  eq(after.item, before.item, 'item kept');\n  eq(after.name, before.name, 'name kept');\n  // Music stays where the player left it, and the flag is ours.\n  assert(!errors.length, errors[0]);\n  await context.close();\n});\n\ntest('WebKit here has no WebGPU: it shows the no-WebGPU page', async () => {\n  const { webkit } = await import('playwright');\n  const browser = await webkit.launch();\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\n  await page.goto(`file://${HTML}`);\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('WebGPU') || window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__, null, { timeout: 30000 });\n  const t = await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText);\n  const hasGpu = await page.evaluate(() => !!navigator.gpu);\n  if (!hasGpu) { assert(t.includes('needs WebGPU'), `page says: ${t.slice(0, 200)}`); assert(t.includes('Diabellical'), 'title on the page'); }\n  await browser.close();\n});\n\ntest('the kit agrees:\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > docs/DESIGNERS.md <<'EOF'\n# Building the rest of the game\n\nEverything a designer touches is plain data in `src/data`, rooms are ASCII, models are `ModelDef`s, songs\nare text patterns. Dev mode (pause menu) tests any of it at once. Run `node tools/build.mjs` then open the\nHTML, and `node tools/test.mjs --sim` tells you if the data refers to something that does not exist.\n\n## Add a monster\n1. Add a row to `MONSTERS` in `src/data/monsters.js`: `hp` and `hit` multiply the level formulas, `ai` names a\n   state machine in `src/sim/monsters.js` (`melee lunge leaper ranged slam bomber hook blinker charger swooper necro plate spawner`).\n2. Add a body to `src/view/models/monsters.js`. Humanoids use `humanoid({...})` and get all hero clips.\n   `node check.mjs --sheets src/view/models/monsters.js` draws it.\n3. Add it to a zone's `monsters` table in `src/data/zones.js`, with a weight.\n4. Dev mode, SPAWN tab, to meet it. Its Bestiary entry appears by itself.\n\n## Add a skill or a Tone\nAdd to `SKILLS` in `src/data/skills.js`. `fx` is a list of ops, and the ops are the whole vocabulary:\n`arc circle cone ring projectile lob chain dash leap blink zone obstacle summon turret buff debuff pull knock\nstun apply_status consume_status consume_graves comet_rain delay repeat spawn_decoy`. A Tone has `patch` (fields\non the skill), `fx` (overrides per op index) and `add` (more ops). Add the id to the class in `src/data/classes.js`.\n\n## Add an item, a legendary, a set, an affix\n`src/data/items.js`. A legendary needs a row in `LEGENDARIES` and a hook object of the same id in\n`src/sim/powers.js`: `onCast`, `onHit`, `onKill`, `onPickup`, `tick`, `modifySkill`.\n\n## Add a room\nAdd an ASCII template to `src/data/rooms/`: `#` wall, `.` floor, `~` water or pit, `P` pillar, `D` door socket,\n`S` trash spawn, `E` elite spawn, `C` chest, `B` breakable, `T` trap, `L` light, `A` shrine, `X` way in or on,\n`N` named prop from the template's `named` list. List it in a zone's `gen.fill`. The tests walk it for 200 seeds.\n\n## Add a zone\nAdd to `ZONES` and `BIOMES` in `src/data/zones.js`, give it a song in `ZONE_SONGS` (`src/data/songs.js`), and\nsomewhere to enter from: a named `exit`, or a line in the Map screen's list and `zoneOpen` in `src/sim/commands.js`.\n\n## Add a quest\nSteps go in `QUESTS` (`src/data/quests.js`). What ends a step goes in `src/sim/quests.js`: `onTalkDone`,\n`onObjectUsed`, `onBossKilled`, `onZoneEntered`, or `stepCheap` for positions. `objectiveOf` tells the map marker\nand the bot where to go. Lines for a step go in `TALKS` in `src/data/dialog.js`, keyed `npc:quest.step`.\n\n## Add a song or a sound\nSongs are `S('D4:4 r:4 A4:2')` strings in `src/data/songs.js`: note and length in steps, `r` is a rest. Every track of a\npattern must add up to the same length (the tests say which one does not). Sounds are `SoundDef`s in `src/data/sfx.js`.\n\n## Tune it\n`src/data/tuning.js` holds the formulas and the sliders. Every row of `TUNING` is a live slider in dev mode.\n`node tools/report.mjs 11,12` plays the campaign with the bot and prints minutes, levels, boss times and drops.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet 2>&1 | tail -n 3; timeout 100 node tools/test.mjs --sim 2>&1 | tail -n 5 | cut -c1-400;timeout 300 node tools/test.mjs --browser \"save\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-500; timeout 100 node tools/test.mjs --browser \"WebKit\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-500","description":"Apply polish batch, add save and WebKit tests, run them","timeout":520000}}}
