{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\n<analysis>\nLet me chronologically go through the conversation and capture everything.\n\n1. User invoked /goal: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" A session-scoped Stop hook blocks stopping until condition holds.\n\n2. STAGE.md: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n\n3. TASK.md key items (must be preserved): SOURCE Diablo 3; title riff chosen by RNG; Package: single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162036].html; tech: riftlight engine kit, keep pixel-engine.js as shipped; audio all code, Animalese voices, music 10%; online: AI Hub; working env: subfolder; \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server, bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks... confirm the page is your game... Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"; Testing: headless tools, scripted playthrough; one command prints only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing code it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check. \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"; Dev mode from pause menu w/ sliders with reset; attract mode after 10 s; multiplayer via hub; 10-foot controller-first UI; touch-only message; No TODOs; Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in chat reply and in-game About/Credits; \"Usage: added on import\"; exit-interview.json beside the html with exact shape; aiHub block.\n\nKeep every file inside own folder, not /tmp; don't run playwright install; 1-2 browsers.\n\nExit interview shape: sourceInformation {date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage}, testingFeedback [4], engineFeedback [6], promptFeedback[4], aiHub{name,tagline,description,type,genre,source,series,players,controls,tags}.\n\nDate 2026-11-05 16:20:36; Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh; Usage: added on import. Plan: PLAN.md. Suggested aiHub values in the plan: tagline `The bell is cracked. The dead are up. So are you.`; description `A gothic hack-and-slash for 1 to 4 players: smash hordes as a Bellwarden, Lamplighter or Sexton, hunt loot that rings like church bells, and silence a furious walled-up saint.`; type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls `Stick or WASD or click to move · Cross or click to attack · face buttons, R1, R2 or right click, 1-4 for skills · L2 or Space to dodge`; tags 3d, co-op, pixel art, fantasy, boss fights, top-down.\n\nsourceInformation per plan: genre \"Co-op action RPG (hack-and-slash)\"; perspective \"Fixed 3/4 isometric, orthographic\"; tech \"Pixel Engine and its version (with three.js and Rapier inside), JavaScript modules bundled with esbuild, WebGPU, Web Audio, the AI Hub session client and its version\" (Pixel Engine 0.46.0; three.js r186; aihub-session 1.4.0); artDirection \"The engine's native pixel-art toon style and palette, with new models for heroes, NPCs, monsters, bosses and key props; the library for generic props\"; animation \"The engine's clip system on its hero rig, new clips, and procedural legs, springs and squash\"; audio \"All in code: chiptune songs, synthesised effects, Animalese-style babble for voices, music at 10% by default\"; online \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, up to 4; couch co-op on its own\"; testing \"headless scripts that play the game and check its state, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to review\"; research \"What you really did. This plan counts; otherwise none\".\n\nQuestions for feedback: Testing: How many issues did testing catch? How many critical? Most helpful test? least helpful test? Engine: liked most; stuck or guess wrong; most important built yourself; hardest part; what changed in engine (none); one thing to change. Prompt: liked most; confusing; hardest; change.\n\n4. Title picked: Diabellical. Dev folder: Diabellical-Diablo3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162036. Deliverable: ../Diabellical-Diablo3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162036.html at root (\"work\" folder). exit-interview.json at root.\n\nWork folder absolute: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162036__x14746a/work/\n\nCurrent working directory now: dev folder.\n\nKit copied; .dl contains downloaded zips. session.js, tools/hub (harness, bridge, round), docs/HUB-README.md.\n\nHashes: pixel-engine 80408b4c..., session 6ab6be43...\n\n5. Written files (all big):\nsrc/data: meta.js, tuning.js, classes.js, skills.js, items.js, monsters.js, zones.js, rooms/{shared,causeway,special}.js, lore.js, dialog.js, quests.js, sfx.js, songs.js, about.generated.js (generated)\nsrc/sim: core.js, intents.js, stats.js, effects.js, powers.js, monsters.js, hazards.js, hero.js, loot.js, zonegen.js, objects.js, travel.js, bosses.js, quests.js, knell.js, round.js, commands.js, world.js, bot.js\nsrc/view: models/{rig,heroes,monsters,npcs,props,index}.js, clips.js, fxkit.js, zonebuild.js, actors.js, vfx.js, view.js, lootview.js, sets.js\nsrc/audio: voice.js, audio.js\nsrc/save/save.js\nsrc/ui: ui.js, glyphs.js, icons.js, hud.js, devoverlays.js, menus/{base,hero,vendors,world,pause,dev,shell}.js\nsrc/input/router.js\nsrc/modes: game.js, attract.js\nsrc/net: codec.js, host.js, client.js, hubflow.js, card.js\ngame.js, tools/build.mjs, tools/browser.mjs, tools/shots.mjs, tools/test.mjs, tools/report.mjs, tools/hubcheck.mjs, tools/exit-interview.draft.json, tests/lib.mjs, tests/sim/all.mjs, tests/headless/{harness,simplay,all}.mjs, tests/browser/all.mjs, tests/hub/all.mjs, tests/ISSUES.md, docs/DESIGNERS.md, package.json, .gitignore, PROGRESS.md at root.\n\nTest status: tier sim all pass (24); headless: all pass except exit interview (not written); last full run of headless had 13 passed, 2 failed (balance: Bursar; exit interview). After that Bursar hp raised to 520, Malison 1500 — balance test not re-confirmed. Playthroughs passed after fix (need to re-run after later changes). Browser: boot, pad-only, mouse (passed after step fix), couch passed, touch, sound passed, layout passed, save passed, WebKit passed, kit check passed. Hub: 5 harness variants + game-level + outside session pass.\n\nIssues noted in tests/ISSUES.md count: let me enumerate:\n1. minor: Collection Plate spill\n2. minor: cells doors\n3. critical: hero blinked/shoved stuck\n4. minor: novice waves spawn in walls\n5. critical: hero's actor never appeared\n6. minor: bot idle\n7. minor: lint banned word\n8. critical: Foreclosure\n9. critical: Dusk Step blink through walls\n10. minor: pad focus\n11. minor: exit attract\n12. critical: bot heroes never finished talking\n13. critical: pantry door missing\n14. critical: physics panic\n15. critical: Bellfall inside wall\n16. critical: Knell run left alive\n17. minor: pad claim seat one\n18. minor: trail NaN\n\nSo 18 lines: criticals: 3,5,8,9,12,13,14,15,16 = 9 critical (12 was bot-only in harness... labelled critical). Also could be more added.\n\nRecent visuals (last shot review): Boss shots show issues to fix:\n- The Bursar shot: boss toast \"THE BURSAR\" big red overlapped with bar and elite toasts (toast stacking is busy). In dev spawn (noIntro) only. Elite pack toasts spam because of dev travels. Fine but the toast for `boss` when !e.intro. Could limit toasts count to 3.\n- Malison shots: In belfry arena shot, Malison isn't visible! Camera: hero at bottom entrance; Malison at center (z.w/2, z.h/2), ~14 m away offscreen (top right corner shows part: halo and ropes at top right at \"boss_malison2\" shows halo; green ropes). Bell rope visible. Arena is dark, and Malison offscreen when at entrance; that's by distance. In phase 1 hero just stood at entrance as no input. OK. But \"the arena floor dark\": Lights from pillars present (cyan). Should check Malison looks by moving hero closer. Rope arms appear green/lime? 'mat sand' color shows green due to lights. Need shot near Malison. Also the arena is big: 33×31; view height 11.5 → boss far from entrance. Could move start closer or do a shot near center.\n- The world floor in the belfry is dark. Could raise light. The `~` around arena uses rift-energy 'wavy' plane; good.\n- Exit stairs model with yellow rails dominates at entries. 'stone-steps' okay-ish.\n- WASD MOVE prompt remains in shots because the hero hasn't moved (`moved` not incremented by god etc). Fine.\n- Toasts overlapped with HUD quest text in the top-right: \"PUT THE PEATWALKERS BACK DOWN\" with long toasts overlap; quest text on right vs. wide toasts. For layout: limit toast width to not overlap minimap: toast wrap width = W - 2*(72+12+8)... at 427: 427-184=243 px → 40 chars. Big toasts scale 2: wrap at 243. Let me fix (wrap toasts within center column) and limit to 3 visible toasts.\n- Top-left: elite names at world-labels overlapping HUD. Minor.\n- Knell gauge OK. Mods text at right of gauge overlapped by big toast. Fine.\n- Upgrade toast w/ long name overflows center and overlapped: need wrap/truncate with prompt.\n- Damage numbers fine. \n- Couch HUD not yet looked at; attract not looked at; title framing not re-looked; touch not looked at; hero select not looked.\n\nRemaining plan items:\n- Look at shots: title, attract, combat with 40+, each zone (done earlier), each class casting (done), Gear/Skills/vendors (done), Map, dialogue (done), each boss (done except near Malison), Knell meter (done), couch HUD (not), dev mode (done), About (done), touch (not).\n- Fix toast layout.\n- exit-interview.json written, rebuild; About test passes with real answers; final full `node tools/test.mjs`.\n- Clean up: `.scratch` in dev folder (contains my scripts & shots), `.build`, node_modules? \"Every file you made inside your folder\". Keep. Should stop processes. A note: rm with glob after cd blocked; deletion of .scratch should be by explicit path, may be blocked; it is fine to leave or remove with absolute path. Removing `.scratch` not necessary but \"Anything unneeded files you made along the way are still on you to clean up\". tools/shots.mjs writes into .scratch/shots (referenced). Could `rm -r /abs/path/.scratch` explicit.\n- The git status: repo root is parent repo; don't commit unless asked. Not asked.\n- Final chat reply must carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n- PROGRESS.md update: mark milestones.\n\nAlso note `.gitignore` in dev.\n\nOther details: `tools/hubcheck.mjs` exports serve, runVariant. Test running commands: `node tools/test.mjs --sim|--headless|--browser|--hub [grep]`, TEST_TIMES=1, TEST_STACK=1. `node tools/build.mjs --quiet`. Long-running commands timeouts: Bash tool max 600000 ms; full test tiers: sim ~10 s; headless ~ up to few minutes; browser ~few minutes; hub ~ 2 min. \n\nAnother note: blocked `rm .scratch/shots/*` after cd by harness (\"Dangerous rm operation detected\") — the whole command incl. python edits didn't run; re-applied without deletion. Note: don't use `rm` globs.\n\nAlso earlier cat with no input hung (my mistake) and wrote /tmp/null - removed.\n\nUser messages: only the /goal command (+ system \"user hasn't heard from you\" reminders—these are system-ish, appears in user-turn? They appear as system messages: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\" These appear as system reminders. I'd mention them as harness nudges: keep brief updates.) Also instruction: \"Before you start, tell the user... While you work, give the user a short update alongside next tool call\".\n\nAttribution: End git commit messages... only if commit asked. Not asked.\n\nImportant in-game design details for future me: game.js exports createGame({fixedSeed:12345,noAttract:true,...}); `DiabellicalGame` in src/modes/game.js; hooks; `game.cmd(c, seat)`; `game.screenClasses`; `game.skipCutscenes`; `game.toggleBot(0)`, `game.memOf(h)`; mem.tour, mem.opts, mem.override; `window.__GAME__`, `window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__`; `ui.drawnText`, `ui.focus`, `ui.lastWidgets`; `game.evCounts`.\n\nPending polish ideas I listed that were done: credits roll; GetUp + coffin burst; couch leash; wheel zoom; footsteps; mon_hurt; tall prop fade; town dressing; Belfry arena lights; class font labels; bone ring; plate per run; DESIGNERS.md; analyzeClip test. All applied (\"Apply polish batch\" ran successfully since that command wasn't the blocked one). Need to verify: yes the polish batch command ran and test results output. The blocked one was the follow-up with tests/shot; re-applied.\n\nWere full tests re-run after polish? Sim passes partially (everything data 1 passed after fix), other tiers need re-run. boneRing for Warden etc. might impact Knell test; need re-run headless. Also CreditsRoll with skipCutscenes skip; ok.\n\nIn tests/headless/all.mjs Shamble test passes now.\n\nNow also the current work: reviewing boss screenshots; found issues. Last message: images s7, s8 read. So next: fix toast layout, view Malison closer, view attract/title/couch/touch shots; write exit-interview.json; rebuild; full tests; final reply.\n\nLet me capture more code detail on what to change for toasts: in src/ui/hud.js `toastsDraw(ui)`: wraps at `ui.w - 60`; start y=44; `toast()` keeps max 5. Prompt toasts not wrapped. Proposed: only draw top 3, wrap to width `ui.w - 2*96`; prompt toast truncated.\n\nAlso the Malison view: consider placing hero entry closer or shot near center: In tools/shots.mjs bosses scenario add moving hero next to Malison before snap. In attract `malison` stop bots fight it, so `attract_5` shot would show.\n\n`tools/shots.mjs` scenarios: title, menu, newhero, play, zones, fight, ui, bosses, classes, attract. Couch and touch shots not yet present: need adding: couch (use pad stub init or dev 'addBotSeat' ×3 → couch HUD), touch (Pixel 7 profile via openGame contextOptions).\n\nTesting Feedback answer data: count lines in tests/ISSUES.md at end (currently 18 lines, 9 critical). Most helpful test: bot whole-game playthrough; least helpful: e.g. tuning default round trip / the template width check. Engine feedback notes: liked: Engine.headless with engine.step and replay fingerprints, model data format + library; stuck/guess wrong: Breakables chunk panic (wasm unreachable) in long sessions - replaced; Trail NaN with identical points; hud.text uppercase; `loadZone` events; `lift` param in gaitClip causing foot slide; Rng.fork; ragdoll root; most important built: sim/net/UI layer immediate mode; hardest: no HUD alpha, 480x270 text budget, debugging through minified engine; changed: none; change one thing: HUD layering/alpha or Breakables robust or per-pad input. Prompt feedback: liked: plan verified facts; confusing: ...; hardest: scope; change: ...\n\nNote `exit-interview` \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\". Research: \"The plan's own notes only; no extra research\" e.g. \"PLAN.md (no further source research)\".\n\nAbout screen: aboutLines clean uppercase; KIT_CREDITS embed. build.mjs reads ../exit-interview.json else tools/exit-interview.draft.json. Must rebuild after writing. Exit interview test forbids 'unknown' in feedback answers. Test on aiHub.name equals TITLE.\n\nControls string contains '·' and '–' in players '1–4' — plain text allowed; About cleans.\n\nAlso note PROGRESS.md milestones unchecked still; should update checkboxes (M0–M8 essentially done).\n\nAlso \"docs/HUB-README.md\" & CREDITS shipping: Credits embedded.\n\nNow write the summary, thorough but well organized. Include key code snippets for recent items. Include constraints verbatim.Summary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user's single request was the `/goal` command: **\"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"** A session Stop hook blocks stopping until this holds, and it clears by itself once the condition is met.\n   - STAGE.md says: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - **Hand-ins, in the work folder `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162036__x14746a/work/`:**\n     - `Diabellical-Diablo3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162036.html`: a single file with engine, code and hub client inlined. Already built by `node tools/build.mjs`; must be rebuilt after the exit interview is written.\n     - `exit-interview.json`: NOT yet written.\n     - The final chat reply must carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback. The same text goes on the in-game About/Credits screen, generated from exit-interview.json by tools/build.mjs.\n   - Dev folder: `.../work/Diabellical-Diablo3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162036/` (this is the current working directory). The title **Diabellical** was picked by a real RNG from 50.\n   - **Constraints from TASK.md and PLAN.md, preserved:**\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks ... and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n     - Keep every file inside your own folder, not /tmp. Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`. Use at most 1-2 browsers at once. \"Target closed\" means memory ran out.\n     - Never edit `pixel-engine.js`. Keep `session.js` byte for byte (a test checks both hashes).\n     - No TODO, placeholder or stub in src. None of the source's names in src (lint). HUD font only: no em dash, ×, or arrows.\n     - Testing goes behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; rerun only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check, but look at every one before finishing (PLAN section 16: \"look at each one at least once\").\n     - Music defaults to 10%. Voices are gibberish. No audio files.\n     - Commit or push only if asked (not asked). Give the user a short update alongside tool calls when starting major work.\n   - Exit interview shape (exact keys): `sourceInformation {date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage}`, `testingFeedback`[4], `engineFeedback`[6], `promptFeedback`[4], `aiHub {name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, series, players, controls, tags}`.\n   - Values to use:\n     - date `2026-11-05 16:20:36`; source `Diablo 3`; plan `PLAN.md`\n     - genre `Co-op action RPG (hack-and-slash)`; perspective `Fixed 3/4 isometric, orthographic`\n     - tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (with three.js r186 and Rapier inside), JavaScript modules bundled with esbuild, WebGPU, Web Audio, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n     - artDirection: `The engine's native pixel-art toon style and palette, with new models for heroes, NPCs, monsters, bosses and key props; the library for generic props`\n     - animation: `The engine's clip system on its hero rig, new clips, and procedural legs, springs and squash`\n     - audio: `All in code: chiptune songs, synthesised effects, Animalese-style babble for voices, music at 10% by default`\n     - online: `AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, up to 4; couch co-op on its own`\n     - testing: headless scripts that play the game and check its state, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to review\n     - research: the plan only (no extra research)\n     - environment `Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux`; model `Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh`; usage exactly `added on import`\n     - aiHub: name `Diabellical`; tagline `The bell is cracked. The dead are up. So are you.`; description `A gothic hack-and-slash for 1 to 4 players: smash hordes as a Bellwarden, Lamplighter or Sexton, hunt loot that rings like church bells, and silence a furious walled-up saint.`; type `Game`; genre `RPG`; source `Diablo 3`; series `Diablo`; players `1–4`; controls `Stick or WASD or click to move · Cross or click to attack · face buttons, R1, R2 or right click, 1-4 for skills · L2 or Space to dodge`; tags `3d, co-op, pixel art, fantasy, boss fights, top-down`\n   - Feedback questions, in order:\n     - Testing: How many issues did testing catch? / How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? / What was the most helpful test you ran? / What was the least helpful test you ran?\n     - Engine: What did you like most about the engine? / Did you get stuck or guess wrong? / What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? / What was the hardest part about using the engine? / What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing) / If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n     - Prompt: What did you like most about this prompt? / What was confusing? / What was the hardest thing to do? / What would you change in this prompt?\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pixel Engine 0.46.0: `Engine.start`, `Engine.headless`, `engine.step`, `renderer.capture`, recordings and fingerprints, `hud` pixel canvas, `buildModel`/`model`/`checkModel`, `compileClips`/`gaitClip`/`analyzeClip`, `Ragdoll`, `Decals`, `Trail`, `ctx.lights` pool, `LegStepper`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `Timeline`, `groundFog`, `Precipitation`, `WaterSurface`, `NavGrid`, `Rng`.\n   - Architecture:\n     - `src/sim` is plain JS. `stepWorld(w, intents[seat])` runs at 60 Hz.\n     - Input becomes Intent: `{mx,mz,ax,az,aimed,tgt,held,pressed,goal}`.\n     - Menu actions go through `applyCommand(w, seat, {c:...})`.\n     - The sim emits `w.events`; `view.consume` and `hudSys.consume` read them, and the host forwards them.\n     - Effect ops (data-driven skills and Tones) live in `src/sim/effects.js`.\n     - Objects use deterministic ids (1000000+) and props 2000000+, so hub clients agree.\n     - One root Rng that never draws, with forks only.\n   - Hub: Session Protocol v1, shared-world. `NetHost`/`NetClient` send messages `i` (10 Hz unreliable), `p` (presses), `c` (commands), `s` (10 Hz under 1,100 bytes), `e` (5 Hz under 12 KB), `d` (hero data 1/s). Own card via `AIHub.connect({card:true})`. A server copy runs `Engine.headless` driven by a timer.\n   - Pause: `engine.timeScale=0` for `freeze` screens (solo and couch). `holdSim` screens (dialogue, cutscene) stop the sim but not time. `covers` screens hide the HUD. Sessions never pause.\n   - Useful debug hooks: `window.__GAME__`, `window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__`, `game.ui.drawnText`, `game.ui.focus`, `game.ui.lastWidgets`, `game.cmd(c, seat)`, `game.toggleBot(0)`, `game.memOf(h)` (`mem.tour`, `mem.opts`, `mem.override`), `game.skipCutscenes`, `game.screenClasses`, `game.evCounts`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder unless noted; all written this session):\n   - `../PROGRESS.md`: progress log with architecture notes. Its milestone checkboxes are still unticked and should be updated.\n   - Kit (unedited): `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs`, `GUIDE.md`, `API.md`, `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md`, etc. `session.js`, `tools/hub/{harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}`, `docs/HUB-README.md`. `.dl/` holds the downloads.\n   - `game.js`: entry. Exports `createGame(opts)` (defaults `{fixedSeed:12345,noAttract:true}`) and `ENGINE_OPTIONS(touchOnly)`. Hub path goes to `src/net/hubflow.js`; a no-WebGPU DOM fatal page is included.\n   - `tools/build.mjs` (`--quiet`): generates `src/data/about.generated.js` from `../exit-interview.json` or else `tools/exit-interview.draft.json` plus CREDITS.md, runs esbuild, and writes the HTML at root with session.js first and the hub metas.\n   - `tools/test.mjs`: one command. `node tools/test.mjs [--sim --headless --browser --hub] [name filter]`; env `TEST_TIMES=1`, `TEST_STACK=1`.\n   - `tools/browser.mjs` (kit flags; `openGame`, `launch`; `TRACE_ERRORS` env).\n   - `tools/hubcheck.mjs` (`serve`, `runVariant`).\n   - `tools/report.mjs` (`node tools/report.mjs 11,12`).\n   - `tools/shots.mjs` (`node tools/shots.mjs title,menu,newhero,play,zones,fight,ui,bosses,classes,attract --size 1280x720`; writes `.scratch/shots`; has `nanScan`). No couch or touch scenario yet.\n   - `tests/lib.mjs`; `tests/sim/all.mjs` (24 tests); `tests/headless/{harness.mjs,simplay.mjs,all.mjs}`; `tests/browser/all.mjs`; `tests/hub/all.mjs`.\n   - `tests/ISSUES.md`: one line per issue a test caught. Currently 18 lines, 9 marked critical. Use the real count at the end.\n   - `src/data/`: `meta, tuning, classes, skills, items, monsters, zones, rooms/{shared,causeway,special}, lore, dialog, quests, sfx, songs, about.generated`.\n     - Boss hp is currently: bursar 520, ambrose 75, malison 1500, cellarer 50, hollow_sexton 150, grand_chorister 130, clapperjaw_prime 170.\n     - Balance edits: flare dmg 1.7 (magnesium 2.6), bone toss 1.3, pallbearers 0.9.\n   - `src/sim/`: `core (slide, unstick), intents, stats, effects, powers, monsters, hazards, hero, loot, zonegen, objects, travel, bosses, quests, knell, round, commands, world, bot`.\n   - `src/view/`: `models/{rig,heroes,monsters,npcs,props,index}, clips, fxkit (own shatter chunks, WaveRing), zonebuild (ZoneView, dressPlace), actors, vfx, view, lootview, sets (ShellSet)`.\n   - `src/audio/{voice,audio}.js`, `src/save/save.js`, `src/input/router.js`.\n   - `src/ui/{ui,glyphs,icons,hud,devoverlays}.js`, `src/ui/menus/{base,hero,vendors,world,pause(+CreditsRoll, AboutScreen),dev,shell}.js`.\n   - `src/modes/{game,attract}.js`, `src/net/{codec,host,client,hubflow,card}.js`.\n   - `docs/DESIGNERS.md` is done.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (the numbers feed the Testing and Engine feedback):\n   - A stray `cat > /tmp/null` hung a Bash call. I stopped it with TaskStop and removed the file.\n   - A harness guard blocked `rm .scratch/shots/*` after a `cd` (\"Dangerous rm operation detected\"), and the whole command, including its python edits, did not run. I reapplied the edits without deleting. **Do not use rm globs after cd.** The screenshots just get overwritten. Any final cleanup should use an explicit absolute path.\n   - Minor fixes: spillGold reference; `cells`/`cloister_walk`/`relic_room` templates (doors into walls, cut-off areas); `openSpot` fallback inside walls; bot idle while boss alive; pad focus scoring (in-line widgets win, disabled skipped for first focus); attract exit firing title any-button (swallow input, don't draw screens during attract unless touch-only); banned words monk and necromancer; `XXX` in glyph art (renamed K); `placeholder` renamed `ghost`; `stub` var renamed `who`; pad claims seat 0 from stick (`beginFrame`).\n   - Critical fixes:\n     - Heroes stuck when overlapping walls: slide unstick branch plus a `unstick()` failsafe for heroes and monsters.\n     - Hero actor missing after loadZone cleared events: `onZone` now calls `makeHero`.\n     - Foreclosure locking heroes out: reopen when any hero is outside; Malison pits now heal after 24 s.\n     - Blink and leap through walls or landing in walls: `castWall` limit, and stay put if not walkable.\n     - Bot talk events read before they happened: handled after `stepWorld`.\n     - Pantry door missing: `road_lych` and `road_gibbets` got bottom sockets; side-room failure retries the layout; test added.\n     - Rapier `wasm unreachable` panic traced to engine `Breakables` in long sessions (not reproducible in isolation): replaced by own ballistic `FxKit.shatter`.\n     - Knell run staying alive in town: `loadZone` nulls `w.run` when leaving the knell zone; `spawnPack` guards an empty table.\n   - Trail NaN vertices when points are identical: push only if moved more than 1e-2 and only if dt>0.\n   - Shamble `lift` param caused foot slip: removed lift; frames 18, stance .62, hip -.05; analyser test passes.\n   - Harness test frame filter matched the harness URL (`game=game.html`): now excludes `page.mainFrame()`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Last known test status:\n     - sim: 24 pass, including lint and data refs.\n     - headless: all three playthroughs and The Last Bell passed, but they were last run before the balance retune to Bursar 520 and Malison 1500 and before the polish batch. The balance test and full tier need rerunning. The exit-interview test fails until the file exists.\n     - browser: all passed individually (boot, pad only, mouse/keys, couch, touch, sound, layout at 3 sizes, save round-trip, WebKit no-WebGPU, kit check).\n     - hub: 5 harness variants, game-level P1/P2, and outside-session all pass.\n   - Balance targets per PLAN: campaign under 75 sim min, level 16–24 at credits, Bursar 60–180 s, Malison 120–300 s, 2+ legendaries (`tests/headless/all.mjs`, seed 11).\n   - Visual reviews done so far: title, menu, new hero, all zones, classes casting, Gear/Skills/Stats/Devotion/Codex, vendors, stash, map, Knell font, pause, about, dialogue, dev, settings, party, bosses, Knell meter.\n   - Issues seen in the last boss shots, not yet fixed:\n     - (a) Toasts are too wide and pile up over the minimap, quest text and mods. `hud.toastsDraw` wraps at `ui.w-60`, start y=44, up to 5 toasts, and upgrade toasts with a prompt don't wrap. Plan: max about 3 visible, wrap to the centre column (about `ui.w - 2*96`), truncate names on prompt toasts.\n     - (b) Malison is off-screen from the arena entrance in the shots, so the boss itself and the arena close-up haven't been seen. Check close up (move the hero near her in the shot, or view attract stop 5), and consider more arena light.\n     - (c) Elite names over HUD corners are minor.\n   - Not yet looked at: title after the framing change (camOverride y and zoom .5), hero select, attract shots, couch HUD, touch screen, credits roll.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.`\n   - No other user-authored instructions. Repeated system nudges said \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue\" (keep giving short updates).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix toast layout (hud.js) and check Malison and arena close up; adjust lighting if needed.\n   - Add couch and touch shot scenarios. Look at title, hero select, attract (6 stops), couch HUD, touch, credits roll at 1920x1080 (or a size the shots run at), and fix anything wrong.\n   - Write `../exit-interview.json` with real answers (counts from tests/ISSUES.md; answers must not be \"unknown\"); `node tools/build.mjs`; confirm the About test passes.\n   - Run the full `node tools/test.mjs` (tiers separately if needed; Bash max 600 s per call) until zero failures, including playthroughs for all three classes, balance, and all hub variants. Log any new issues in tests/ISSUES.md and keep the interview counts honest; rebuild after any answer change.\n   - Confirm the deliverable runs on file:// and from a server (tests cover this).\n   - Clean up: stop any processes I started; remove unneeded scratch files (`.scratch` holds scripts and shots; tools/shots.mjs writes there, so recreate on need) via an explicit path if allowed. Update PROGRESS.md milestones.\n   - Final chat reply with Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback (same text as the file).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was reviewing screenshots for \"Done means: you looked at every screenshot\". The last step ran `node tools/shots.mjs bosses --size 1280x720` and read the contact sheets `.scratch/shots/s7.png` (Bursar, Ambrose, Malison phases 1–3, Cellarer) and `s8.png` (Knell meter at 60%, Hollow Sexton, Grand Chorister, Clapperjaw Prime). The bosses render, bars with phase ticks work, the gauge reads well, Requiem and upgrade toasts show. The problems found are the toast overlap and Malison being off-screen from the entrance (see section 5). The previous step fixed Trail NaN and Shamble, and the build is current as of those fixes.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the \"look at every shot and polish\" pass. Fix `toastsDraw` in `src/ui/hud.js` (limit and wrap to the centre column), rebuild with `node tools/build.mjs --quiet`, and shoot Malison close up plus the title, attract, couch and touch screens. Then write `../exit-interview.json`, rebuild, run the full `node tools/test.mjs`, and finish with the final reply carrying the four required sections. This serves the goal: \"Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-162036--x14746a-work/74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"73aa6e7e-13b0-45f8-a74f-d0e11107334f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:31:13.913Z","isSynthetic":true}
