{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkpQ1uSYSidJ1oCyGHZY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ra1ckow1tjmt4hXtrHn6tq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162036__x14746a/work/PLAN.md","offset":1015,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4186,"cache_read_input_tokens":100835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4186},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"35ec7778-6161-47a9-9da6-950233b975e5","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:37:05.485Z","request_id":"req_011CgkpQ1f4Nc8jiCbodGHE9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ra1ckow1tjmt4hXtrHn6tq":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162036__x14746a/work/PLAN.md","offset":1015,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ra1ckow1tjmt4hXtrHn6tq","type":"tool_result","content":"1015\t## 15. Build order\n1016\t\n1017\tFinish each milestone before the next. The deliverable builds and runs after each one. Run the tier of tests that covers what you changed.\n1018\t\n1019\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n1020\t|---|---|---|\n1021\t| **M0** | **Setup.** Title picked, dev folder made. Kit unpacked, `session.js` and hub files fetched, `npm i -D playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder, `tools/build.mjs`, `tools/test.mjs`, an empty game. Start `tests/ISSUES.md` (section 17) | The HTML boots on `file://` in Playwright with the right flags; `node check.mjs --headless game.js` passes |\n1022\t| **M1** | **One good room.** Sim, intents, one Bellwarden with Clout and Great Toll, Peatwalkers, keyboard and mouse and pad, candle, action bar, numbers, ragdolls, shattering props, gold, Tallow | It's fun to hit things for a minute. A sim test kills 20 monsters with a bot. Replay matches |\n1023\t| **M2** | **Zone pipeline.** ASCII rooms, generator, wall rule, textures, lights, Ossuary floor, `NavGrid` chase, telegraphs, dodge | Path test passes for 200 seeds. A 1080p shot reads |\n1024\t| **M3** | **All three classes.** Effect ops, all 8 skills per class, Tones, Vows, resources, unlocks, Skills screen. Loopback net test (host and mirror in Node) | Bot uses every skill and Tone without error. Mirror test passes |\n1025\t| **M4** | **Loot.** Items, affixes, rarities, beams, Gear screen, compare, equip, visible weapons and helms, legendaries, sets, Pennywhistle, Brasse, Ogive, gems, stash, save and load | Bot finds and equips upgrades. Save round-trips. Menu flow test by pad and by mouse |\n1026\t| **M5** | **The campaign.** All zones, quests, dialogue, voices, town, Lychgates, Passing Bell, Requiem, shrines, coffins, Plate, elites, bosses, cutscenes, full music and SFX | Whole-game playthrough passes for all three classes |\n1027\t| **M6** | **Multiplayer.** Couch seats and camera, Pyx. Hub flow, netcode, own card, the round | Harness passes in all 5 variants. A game test sees P2's hero move in P1's world. Pad stubs drive 4 seats |\n1028\t| **M7** | **Endgame.** Knell Runs, Grand Knell, Penance, Devotion, Writs, The Last Bell start | Bot clears a Knell Run on each class |\n1029\t| **M8** | **The shell.** Title, menu, hero select, settings, attract, dev mode, Codex, How to Play, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU | All shell tests pass. Every screen shot looks right at three sizes |\n1030\t| **M9** | **Finish.** Balance with `tools/report.mjs` and sliders, a look at every shot, more lines, more juice, exit interview, a final build that carries its answers | Definition of done |\n1031\t\n1032\t**Do M6 after M5 but keep the seams from M1:** the mirror test in M3 proves the split early.\n1033\t\n1034\t### If you must cut\n1035\t\n1036\tWhole features only, in this order, and remove every trace: Writs → Drowned Pantry → Gems → Devotion → Vows → Grand Knell → Sister Pyx → Reliquary extraction → Lore books (keep How to Play) → the round's level-up picks → the third class's last 2 skills.\n1037\t\n1038\t**Never cut:** three classes, Tones, loot rarities with beams, legendaries, town services, five quests, three bosses, Knell Runs, couch co-op, hub sessions, pad-first UI, glyph switching, attract, dev mode with sliders, About, voices, music at 10%, the playthrough test.\n1039\t\n1040\t---\n1041\t\n1042\t## 16. Testing\n1043\t\n1044\t`node tools/test.mjs` runs everything and prints **only failures and one count line**. `--sim`, `--headless`, `--browser`, `--hub` run one tier; rerun only the tier that covers what you changed. Use at most two browsers at once, sequentially. Serve from `127.0.0.1` on port 0 inside the test process, confirm the page's title is yours, and stop only what you started. \"Target closed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out: run fewer at once. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge.\n1045\t\n1046\t### Tier 1: sim (Node, no engine loop, seconds)\n1047\t\n1048\t- `stepWorld` is deterministic: same seed and intents, same hash, for 5 minutes of play.\n1049\t- Damage, armour, XP curve, item generation stay inside ranges; items always valid. Each effect op works. Each legendary's hook fires. Each Affliction behaves.\n1050\t- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone. The same seed builds an identical map no matter what other streams have drawn (section 2, item 31).\n1051\t- **Net:** host plus mirrors over a simulated lossy transport (150 ms, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss) in Node: mirrors converge, commands arrive, budgets respected (message rate under 20 a second, `s` under 1,100 bytes, `e` under 12 KB).\n1052\t- **Lint:** every string in `src/data` fits the HUD font; line lengths fit; no `Math.random` or `performance.now` in `src/sim`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub` or `coming soon` anywhere in `src`; none of the banned names from section 1; every `use`, texture, clip, sound and song referenced by data exists; `validateClip` clean on every clip; `renderSound` non-silent and peak ≤ 1 for every sound; `parseSong` on every song.\n1053\t- `checkModel` has zero problems on every model.\n1054\t- `pixel-engine.js` and `session.js` are byte-identical to what you downloaded (keep their hashes in `tools/`).\n1055\t\n1056\t### Tier 2: the game in `Engine.headless` (Node, a minute or two)\n1057\t\n1058\t- `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys ...` with keys that really play. Replay matches.\n1059\t- **Whole-game playthrough, once per class, default tuning, Pilgrim:** the bot (`tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`) starts at the title, makes a hero through the real menus by keys, plays to the credits by intents and commands. Asserts: every zone visited; every quest done; all three bosses killed; every skill slot used; a legendary equipped; item salvaged, crafted, reforged, sold, bought, stashed, extracted, socketed; every Lychgate touched; a shrine and a coffin used; ending played; Knell Runs unlocked; then one full Knell Run. Every row of the feature table in section 3 that the campaign can reach must have happened. Fail on any softlock (no progress for 3 sim minutes).\n1060\t- **The Last Bell, once per class:** start it through the menus, spend Devotion, change tier, complete a Grand Knell, see a set bonus apply. This covers the table's remaining rows.\n1061\t- **Balance report:** `tools/report.mjs` prints minutes per zone, deaths, level at each zone, boss durations, drops by rarity. Assert: campaign under 75 sim minutes; level 16 to 24 at the credits; the Bursar 60 to 180 s; Malison 120 to 300 s; 2+ legendaries.\n1062\t- **Screens:** every menu opens, navigates, closes, by keyboard codes. `ui.drawnText` has what it should. Dev mode: every tool and slider has an effect, and Reset restores.\n1063\t- **Attract:** idle 600 frames on the title: attract starts. Idle on the main menu: same. Any key exits. It loops twice with no errors, covering each stop. Saves untouched.\n1064\t- **About:** every Source Information label and every feedback question and answer appears in `ui.drawnText` across the pages, and Usage reads `added on import`.\n1065\t- **Exit interview, once written:** parses as JSON; has exactly the keys in section 17; 4, 6 and 4 feedback answers; `aiHub.name` equals `TITLE`; 3 to 6 lowercase tags; no empty values, except that `series` may be empty.\n1066\t- **Audio:** `audio.volume.music === 0.1` on first run, and after Reset. Every zone starts its song. Speaking a line increases counts and its syllables are the same each time.\n1067\t\n1068\t### Tier 3: browser (real WebGPU on SwiftShader)\n1069\t\n1070\tUse the flags in section 2 item 5. Open the bundle over `file://`, use `engine.step` and `capture`, and don't wait in real time.\n1071\t\n1072\t- **Boot:** no page, console, game or GPU errors. Picture isn't blank (`capture`). The bundle is one file: `session.js` byte-identical and first; metas present.\n1073\t- **Pad only** (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads` in standard mapping via `addInitScript`): press through title, hero select, play, skills, Hero screen, pause, dev mode, settings, quit. PlayStation glyphs shown (`ui` reports the glyph set). Xbox option switches them. A key press switches prompts to keycaps; a pad press switches back.\n1074\t- **Mouse and keyboard only:** hover moves focus (`page.mouse.move` over a menu item, `ui.focus` changes); click activates; click-to-move moves; click on a monster attacks; every key in section 10 works.\n1075\t- **Couch:** 4 stub pads join, each moves its own hero, camera holds them.\n1076\t- **Touch:** Chromium with a phone profile (Pixel 7) and a tablet profile, tapping with `page.touchscreen`: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. A tap doesn't start a game. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so it can only confirm the no-WebGPU page.\n1077\t- **Sound, by what Web Audio produces:** the engine doesn't expose its output node, so wrap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in `addInitScript` to also feed anything connected to the destination into an `AnalyserNode`. After a key press unlocks audio: music alone gives a non-zero level; a sound effect raises it well above that; a spoken line produces sound; `end` in a session brings it to silence.\n1078\t- **Layout:** `ui.drawnText` rectangles stay inside the screen at 1280×720, 1920×1080, 2560×1440, with no overlaps on each screen.\n1079\t- **Screenshots** for your own eyes (`tools/shots.mjs`, at 1920×1080): title, attract, combat with 40+ monsters, each zone, each class casting, Gear, Skills, each vendor, Map, dialogue, each boss, Knell meter, couch HUD, dev mode, About, touch. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check: look at each one at least once before finishing.\n1080\t\n1081\t### Tier 4: hub\n1082\t\n1083\tCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` beside a copy of the deliverable and serve them on `127.0.0.1` port 0. Open and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`:\n1084\t\n1085\t1. `?game=GAME&players=2&auto=1`\n1086\t2. `?game=GAME&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1087\t3. The same with `&scenario=host-leave`\n1088\t4. `?game=GAME&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n1089\t5. `?game=GAME&players=1&auto=1`\n1090\t\n1091\tThen a **game-level** check: two frames, drive P2 by synthetic keys inside its frame, and read `frame.contentWindow.__GAME__` to see P2's hero move in P1's world and P1's in P2's. Then outside a session: the page opened on its own still plays normally.\n1092\t\n1093\t---\n1094\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"be3096d1-1a9d-4b5c-ad23-ead4560f2f0b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:37:05.497Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162036__x14746a/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 15. Build order\n\nFinish each milestone before the next. The deliverable builds and runs after each one. Run the tier of tests that covers what you changed.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | **Setup.** Title picked, dev folder made. Kit unpacked, `session.js` and hub files fetched, `npm i -D playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder, `tools/build.mjs`, `tools/test.mjs`, an empty game. Start `tests/ISSUES.md` (section 17) | The HTML boots on `file://` in Playwright with the right flags; `node check.mjs --headless game.js` passes |\n| **M1** | **One good room.** Sim, intents, one Bellwarden with Clout and Great Toll, Peatwalkers, keyboard and mouse and pad, candle, action bar, numbers, ragdolls, shattering props, gold, Tallow | It's fun to hit things for a minute. A sim test kills 20 monsters with a bot. Replay matches |\n| **M2** | **Zone pipeline.** ASCII rooms, generator, wall rule, textures, lights, Ossuary floor, `NavGrid` chase, telegraphs, dodge | Path test passes for 200 seeds. A 1080p shot reads |\n| **M3** | **All three classes.** Effect ops, all 8 skills per class, Tones, Vows, resources, unlocks, Skills screen. Loopback net test (host and mirror in Node) | Bot uses every skill and Tone without error. Mirror test passes |\n| **M4** | **Loot.** Items, affixes, rarities, beams, Gear screen, compare, equip, visible weapons and helms, legendaries, sets, Pennywhistle, Brasse, Ogive, gems, stash, save and load | Bot finds and equips upgrades. Save round-trips. Menu flow test by pad and by mouse |\n| **M5** | **The campaign.** All zones, quests, dialogue, voices, town, Lychgates, Passing Bell, Requiem, shrines, coffins, Plate, elites, bosses, cutscenes, full music and SFX | Whole-game playthrough passes for all three classes |\n| **M6** | **Multiplayer.** Couch seats and camera, Pyx. Hub flow, netcode, own card, the round | Harness passes in all 5 variants. A game test sees P2's hero move in P1's world. Pad stubs drive 4 seats |\n| **M7** | **Endgame.** Knell Runs, Grand Knell, Penance, Devotion, Writs, The Last Bell start | Bot clears a Knell Run on each class |\n| **M8** | **The shell.** Title, menu, hero select, settings, attract, dev mode, Codex, How to Play, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU | All shell tests pass. Every screen shot looks right at three sizes |\n| **M9** | **Finish.** Balance with `tools/report.mjs` and sliders, a look at every shot, more lines, more juice, exit interview, a final build that carries its answers | Definition of done |\n\n**Do M6 after M5 but keep the seams from M1:** the mirror test in M3 proves the split early.\n\n### If you must cut\n\nWhole features only, in this order, and remove every trace: Writs → Drowned Pantry → Gems → Devotion → Vows → Grand Knell → Sister Pyx → Reliquary extraction → Lore books (keep How to Play) → the round's level-up picks → the third class's last 2 skills.\n\n**Never cut:** three classes, Tones, loot rarities with beams, legendaries, town services, five quests, three bosses, Knell Runs, couch co-op, hub sessions, pad-first UI, glyph switching, attract, dev mode with sliders, About, voices, music at 10%, the playthrough test.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing\n\n`node tools/test.mjs` runs everything and prints **only failures and one count line**. `--sim`, `--headless`, `--browser`, `--hub` run one tier; rerun only the tier that covers what you changed. Use at most two browsers at once, sequentially. Serve from `127.0.0.1` on port 0 inside the test process, confirm the page's title is yours, and stop only what you started. \"Target closed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out: run fewer at once. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge.\n\n### Tier 1: sim (Node, no engine loop, seconds)\n\n- `stepWorld` is deterministic: same seed and intents, same hash, for 5 minutes of play.\n- Damage, armour, XP curve, item generation stay inside ranges; items always valid. Each effect op works. Each legendary's hook fires. Each Affliction behaves.\n- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone. The same seed builds an identical map no matter what other streams have drawn (section 2, item 31).\n- **Net:** host plus mirrors over a simulated lossy transport (150 ms, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss) in Node: mirrors converge, commands arrive, budgets respected (message rate under 20 a second, `s` under 1,100 bytes, `e` under 12 KB).\n- **Lint:** every string in `src/data` fits the HUD font; line lengths fit; no `Math.random` or `performance.now` in `src/sim`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub` or `coming soon` anywhere in `src`; none of the banned names from section 1; every `use`, texture, clip, sound and song referenced by data exists; `validateClip` clean on every clip; `renderSound` non-silent and peak ≤ 1 for every sound; `parseSong` on every song.\n- `checkModel` has zero problems on every model.\n- `pixel-engine.js` and `session.js` are byte-identical to what you downloaded (keep their hashes in `tools/`).\n\n### Tier 2: the game in `Engine.headless` (Node, a minute or two)\n\n- `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys ...` with keys that really play. Replay matches.\n- **Whole-game playthrough, once per class, default tuning, Pilgrim:** the bot (`tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`) starts at the title, makes a hero through the real menus by keys, plays to the credits by intents and commands. Asserts: every zone visited; every quest done; all three bosses killed; every skill slot used; a legendary equipped; item salvaged, crafted, reforged, sold, bought, stashed, extracted, socketed; every Lychgate touched; a shrine and a coffin used; ending played; Knell Runs unlocked; then one full Knell Run. Every row of the feature table in section 3 that the campaign can reach must have happened. Fail on any softlock (no progress for 3 sim minutes).\n- **The Last Bell, once per class:** start it through the menus, spend Devotion, change tier, complete a Grand Knell, see a set bonus apply. This covers the table's remaining rows.\n- **Balance report:** `tools/report.mjs` prints minutes per zone, deaths, level at each zone, boss durations, drops by rarity. Assert: campaign under 75 sim minutes; level 16 to 24 at the credits; the Bursar 60 to 180 s; Malison 120 to 300 s; 2+ legendaries.\n- **Screens:** every menu opens, navigates, closes, by keyboard codes. `ui.drawnText` has what it should. Dev mode: every tool and slider has an effect, and Reset restores.\n- **Attract:** idle 600 frames on the title: attract starts. Idle on the main menu: same. Any key exits. It loops twice with no errors, covering each stop. Saves untouched.\n- **About:** every Source Information label and every feedback question and answer appears in `ui.drawnText` across the pages, and Usage reads `added on import`.\n- **Exit interview, once written:** parses as JSON; has exactly the keys in section 17; 4, 6 and 4 feedback answers; `aiHub.name` equals `TITLE`; 3 to 6 lowercase tags; no empty values, except that `series` may be empty.\n- **Audio:** `audio.volume.music === 0.1` on first run, and after Reset. Every zone starts its song. Speaking a line increases counts and its syllables are the same each time.\n\n### Tier 3: browser (real WebGPU on SwiftShader)\n\nUse the flags in section 2 item 5. Open the bundle over `file://`, use `engine.step` and `capture`, and don't wait in real time.\n\n- **Boot:** no page, console, game or GPU errors. Picture isn't blank (`capture`). The bundle is one file: `session.js` byte-identical and first; metas present.\n- **Pad only** (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads` in standard mapping via `addInitScript`): press through title, hero select, play, skills, Hero screen, pause, dev mode, settings, quit. PlayStation glyphs shown (`ui` reports the glyph set). Xbox option switches them. A key press switches prompts to keycaps; a pad press switches back.\n- **Mouse and keyboard only:** hover moves focus (`page.mouse.move` over a menu item, `ui.focus` changes); click activates; click-to-move moves; click on a monster attacks; every key in section 10 works.\n- **Couch:** 4 stub pads join, each moves its own hero, camera holds them.\n- **Touch:** Chromium with a phone profile (Pixel 7) and a tablet profile, tapping with `page.touchscreen`: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. A tap doesn't start a game. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so it can only confirm the no-WebGPU page.\n- **Sound, by what Web Audio produces:** the engine doesn't expose its output node, so wrap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in `addInitScript` to also feed anything connected to the destination into an `AnalyserNode`. After a key press unlocks audio: music alone gives a non-zero level; a sound effect raises it well above that; a spoken line produces sound; `end` in a session brings it to silence.\n- **Layout:** `ui.drawnText` rectangles stay inside the screen at 1280×720, 1920×1080, 2560×1440, with no overlaps on each screen.\n- **Screenshots** for your own eyes (`tools/shots.mjs`, at 1920×1080): title, attract, combat with 40+ monsters, each zone, each class casting, Gear, Skills, each vendor, Map, dialogue, each boss, Knell meter, couch HUD, dev mode, About, touch. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check: look at each one at least once before finishing.\n\n### Tier 4: hub\n\nCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` beside a copy of the deliverable and serve them on `127.0.0.1` port 0. Open and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`:\n\n1. `?game=GAME&players=2&auto=1`\n2. `?game=GAME&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n3. The same with `&scenario=host-leave`\n4. `?game=GAME&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n5. `?game=GAME&players=1&auto=1`\n\nThen a **game-level** check: two frames, drive P2 by synthetic keys inside its frame, and read `frame.contentWindow.__GAME__` to see P2's hero move in P1's world and P1's in P2's. Then outside a session: the page opened on its own still plays normally.\n\n---\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1015,"totalLines":1226}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ra1ckow1tjmt4hXtrHn6tq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
