{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkqaE45mCHbt1YRHM9gr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nhy2bVVALoFHsFh8fQfWBa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > .scratch/hudw.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { boot } from '../tests/headless/harness.mjs';\nconst { game } = await boot({ seed: 1 });\nconsole.log('hud', game.ctx.hud.width, game.ctx.hud.height);\nprocess.exit(0);\nEOF\ntimeout 60 node .scratch/hudw.mjs 2>&1 | tail -n 1; grep -c \"screenshot\" tests/ISSUES.md; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"25. Each one is a line in tests/ISSUES.md: 18 from the scripted tests and 7 from looking at screenshots.\",\n \"10. They include The Way Home spawning inside a wall (a Knell Run with no exit), the Bursar's Foreclosure walls locking a hero out of the fight, blinks through walls, a missing door to the Drowned Pantry, heroes stuck in walls, and a physics panic in long sessions.\",\n \"The whole-game playthrough, once per class, played by a bot through the real menus. It found the stuck heroes, the missing Pantry door and a Knell Run left alive in town, none of which a unit test would have reached. Its sibling, The Last Bell run, found the walled-in exit on the final pass.\",\n \"The tuning check that defaults round-trip and every slider has a home. It never caught anything, because that code hardly changed after it was written.\"]\ne=d['engineFeedback']\ne[0]=\"The headless engine. Engine.headless and engine.step let one test file play the entire campaign through the real game object with no browser, in about a minute per class. Second place goes to models and clips as plain data: every hero, monster and boss here is data the engine's own checker can lint.\"\ne[3]=e[3].replace(\"a 480-pixel-wide HUD\",\"a HUD about 427 art pixels wide at 16:9\")\nd['engineFeedback']=e\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nprint(e[3][:120])\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet; TEST_TIMES=1 timeout 60 node tools/test.mjs --headless \"About\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-300; TEST_TIMES=1 timeout 60 node tools/test.mjs --headless \"exit interview\" 2>&1 | tail -n 2 | cut -c1-300; sed -n '/about:/,/+6p/p' tools/shots.mjs | head -n 0; grep -n \"about\\|'ui'\\|  ui:\" tools/shots.mjs | head -n 6 | cut -c1-180","description":"Correct feedback text, rebuild, recheck About and shape","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":133705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1017},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74a13398-df38-49ac-bc09-f0d3ed7fa96a","uuid":"bb769c49-b9f2-4b26-8745-c9357569f89e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:52:42.135Z","request_id":"req_011CgkqaDhWSV86AuRdw775N","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Nhy2bVVALoFHsFh8fQfWBa":{"command":"cat > .scratch/hudw.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { boot } from '../tests/headless/harness.mjs';\nconst { game } = await boot({ seed: 1 });\nconsole.log('hud', game.ctx.hud.width, game.ctx.hud.height);\nprocess.exit(0);\nEOF\ntimeout 60 node .scratch/hudw.mjs 2>&1 | tail -n 1; grep -c \"screenshot\" tests/ISSUES.md; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"25. Each one is a line in tests/ISSUES.md: 18 from the scripted tests and 7 from looking at screenshots.\",\n \"10. They include The Way Home spawning inside a wall (a Knell Run with no exit), the Bursar's Foreclosure walls locking a hero out of the fight, blinks through walls, a missing door to the Drowned Pantry, heroes stuck in walls, and a physics panic in long sessions.\",\n \"The whole-game playthrough, once per class, played by a bot through the real menus. It found the stuck heroes, the missing Pantry door and a Knell Run left alive in town, none of which a unit test would have reached. Its sibling, The Last Bell run, found the walled-in exit on the final pass.\",\n \"The tuning check that defaults round-trip and every slider has a home. It never caught anything, because that code hardly changed after it was written.\"]\ne=d['engineFeedback']\ne[0]=\"The headless engine. Engine.headless and engine.step let one test file play the entire campaign through the real game object with no browser, in about a minute per class. Second place goes to models and clips as plain data: every hero, monster and boss here is data the engine's own checker can lint.\"\ne[3]=e[3].replace(\"a 480-pixel-wide HUD\",\"a HUD about 427 art pixels wide at 16:9\")\nd['engineFeedback']=e\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nprint(e[3][:120])\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet; TEST_TIMES=1 timeout 60 node tools/test.mjs --headless \"About\" 2>&1 | tail -n 3 | cut -c1-300; TEST_TIMES=1 timeout 60 node tools/test.mjs --headless \"exit interview\" 2>&1 | tail -n 2 | cut -c1-300; sed -n '/about:/,/+6p/p' tools/shots.mjs | head -n 0; grep -n \"about\\|'ui'\\|  ui:\" tools/shots.mjs | head -n 6 | cut -c1-180","description":"Correct feedback text, rebuild, recheck About and shape","timeout":180000}}}
